'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—151''''' (Japanese: '''{{j|強化拡張パック ポケモンカード{{ruby|151|イチゴーイチ}}}}''' ''Enhanced Expansion Pack: Pokémon Card 151'') is the first special expansion released during the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The expansion focuses only on the first 151 Pokémon to ever be introduced; namely, [[Generation I]] Pokémon.

==Blurb==
<i>[[Gotta catch 'em all!|Gotta Catch ’Em All!]]

Team up with Bulbasaur, Charmander, and Squirtle, and witness a brand-new dawn in Kanto! With this new day comes a new chance to track down old friends, make new partners, and capture every last one of the original 151. Discover the extraordinary Venusaur ex, Charizard ex, and Blastoise ex in special cards with captivating illustrations, and explore the cities and countryside of a reinvigorated land—you might even find the elusive Mew ex in your travels. New adventures will unfold and new horizons will be revealed in the Scarlet & Violet—151 expansion!</i>

==Information==
[[File:SV2a Pokémon Card 151 Logo.png|200px|thumb|Pokémon Card 151 logo]]
'''Scarlet & Violet—151''' is a special expansion containing 210 cards that was released on September 22, 2023. In Japan, it is known as '''Pokémon Card 151''', and was released on June 16, 2023, followed by localized releases in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}} on June 30, 2023, and in {{pmin|Indonesia}}, {{pmin|Thailand}} and {{pmin|South Korea}} on July 28, 2023.

151 features only [[Generation I]] Pokémon; unlike in most expansions, Pokémon cards in this expansion are ordered according to the Pokémon's [[National Pokédex]] [[List of Pokémon by National Pokédex number|numbers]], instead of being grouped by their type.<ref>[https://www.pokemon.com/us/pokemon-tcg/scarlet-violet-151/explore-and-watch/ Scarlet & Violet—151] — Pokemon.com</ref> This expansion contains 12 {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} cards, 16 {{TCG|illustration rare}} and seven {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, 16 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards. Cosmos Holofoil {{TCG|SVE Basic Energies|Basic Energy cards}} can also be found in 151 booster packs. There's also a low probability to find an entire evolutionary line of Bulbasaur, Charmander, or Squirtle as secret cards in the same booster pack, in place of the two Reverse Holo cards and the Rare card. Fans refer to such packs as "demigod packs". In the English set and the languages following the English set structure, all Rares and below are also available as Reverse Holofoil versions.

In the Japanese, Korean and Traditional Chinese subsets, each booster pack contains seven cards with two guaranteed Holofoil cards, and common, uncommon, and rare cards have Mirror Holofoil variants featuring a {{i|Poké Ball}} pattern; or, rarely, a [[Master Ball]] pattern. There is also a rare chance for those packs to contain two of the Bulbasaur, Charmander, or Squirtle's entire evolutionary lines as secret cards. Thai and Indonesian booster packs contain five cards with no guarantees of Holofoil cards, and has no Mirror Holofoil prints. 

This subset is notable for introducing the first {{TCG|Kadabra}} card since the release of {{TCG ID|Skyridge|Kadabra|69}} from {{TCG|Skyridge}} in 2003, twenty years prior.

