'''Pokémon TCG: ''30th Celebration''''' (Japanese: '''30th セレブレーション''' ''30th CELEBRATION'') is a special expansion of cards in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. Releasing simultaneously worldwide on September 16, 2026 during the Mega Evolution Series and MEGA Series, it is part of the [[Pokémon 30th Anniversary]] celebrations.

==Blurb==
<i>Celebrating 30 Years of Pokémon

Commemorate 30 years of joy with fan-favorite Pokémon spanning three dazzling decades! Celebrate this magnificent milestone with the mighty presences of Mewtwo ex and Mew ex, followed by a wealth of allies like Umbreon ex, Salamence ex, and Greninja ex. Plus, there are 30 reasons to honor Pikachu, as each booster pack contains one—with 30 unique variations to collect as Pikachu rare cards! And, whether you’re looking forward to a glittering future or taking a nostalgic look at a storied past, there are a host of treasures to find and secrets to reveal in the Pokémon TCG: ''30th Celebration''!</i>

==Information==
Initially teased on [[Pokémon Day#2026|Pokémon Day 2026]], '''30th Celebration''' specifically marks 30 years of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], which debuted in Japan with the {{TCG|Expansion Pack}} (known outside Japan as the {{TCG|Base Set}}) in October 1996. Every single card included in this set, including {{TCG|Basic Energy card}}s, is Holofoil, and almost all of them feature the [[Pokémon 30th Anniversary]] logo.

The 30th Celebration set and its associated products have a general "day" and "night" theme, with many cards in the expansion having daytime and nighttime equivalents of each other. The set also includes a uniquely numbered subset of 30 "{{TCG|Pikachu rare card|Pikachu rare}}" {{p|Pikachu}} cards, with a different holofoil pattern and the Pokémon 30th Anniversary logo behind the card text; each booster pack of 30th Celebration includes one Pikachu rare card.

Additionally, the set introduces {{TCG|Futuristic rare card}}s (identified with the {{rar|Futuristic Rare}} symbol internationally and the {{rar|FUR}} rarity symbol in Asian markets). Futuristic rare cards are indicated by the use of vivid colors and lighting on the Pokémon, as well as 3D graphical elements of Energy and Poké Balls on the card artwork. Futuristic rare cards in this expansion, as well as the Basic Energy cards which share the same artistic style, are illustrated by artist [[YOSHIROTTEN]], who was also responsible for the key visual of the 30th Celebration expansion as a whole. Also introduced and illustrated by YOSHIROTTEN are {{TCG|RGB rare card}}s, {{TCG|secret card}}s identified by the {{rar|RGB Rare}} symbol and a highly-saturated {{3v2|Red|Green|Blue}} color scheme.

Finally, this set features a "{{TCG|Classic Collection}}" of 30 reprinted cards from previous Pokémon Trading Card Game sets, from Base Set to the modern day. All 30 cards featured in the Classic Collection feature a sparkling golden border.

The international 30th Celebration expansion includes cards released in the Japanese 30th Celebration expansion and the {{TCG|30th Celebration Premium Deck Set Espeon & Umbreon}} product.

30th Celebration is the first set to be released globally on the same day—including in Simplified Chinese, which was still catching up with Scarlet & Violet Series sets at the time of the set's release. Each booster pack of 30th Celebration contains 5 cards, one of which is one of the 30 Pikachu rare cards, plus an additional Basic Energy card.

