'''Scarlet & Violet: Ancient Times, Future Progress''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 亘古开来''') is the first {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet Series, and the ninth main expansion overall.

== Information ==
{{main|Scarlet & Violet (TCG)|section=Information}}
'''Ancient Times, Future Progress''' was the first Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game; as such, it introduced [[Generation IX]] Pokémon and new mechanics such as {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} to the game, while {{TCG|Pokémon Tool card}}s were reclassified as their own category of {{TCG|Trainer card}}, rather than a subset of {{TCG|Item card}}s as they were previously.

Like previous expansions released in the Simplified Chinese language, due to the TCG being behind other regions (by approximately two years at this point),<ref name="releasegap"/> the expansion contained cards from across several early Scarlet & Violet Series expansions; however, this expansion did not comprise any subsets, with the same set of cards being available from all booster packs.

Starting with this set, 25-card booster packs were replaced with 20-card booster packs, though the price of each pack remained the same. 5-card packs remained unchanged. Therefore, cards were available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card was either Reverse Holofoil or had a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards were either Reverse Holofoil or had a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 113 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion came in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and one with a rarer Master Ball motif:

