'''Another World''' (Korean: '''또 다른 세계''' ''Tto Dareun Segye'') is the name given to the fourth extension set of cards from the DP Series of the {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The set continues to feature {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}}. {{ct|Fire}} and {{ct|Metal}} are the only types left out that were present in previous sets.

==Information==
'''Another World''' is the fourth Korean extension set of cards after the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] went into hiatus until the middle of 2010. Released September 16, 2010, this extension set continues to introduce both new [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and new {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the Korean Card Game. This set has a large variety of card types, it contains all the types that were previously released except for {{ct|Fire}} and {{ct|Metal}}.

Included in the Another World set are 40 cards originating from the early half of the English Diamond & Pearl Series. The set pulls its {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} focus from the {{TCG|Platinum}} and {{TCG|Mysterious Treasures}} expansions, but contains a majority of cards from the {{TCG|Diamond & Pearl}} and {{TCG|Mysterious Treasures}} expansions. {{TCG ID|POP Series 8|Luxray|3}} is the only one coming from {{TCG|POP Series 8}}.

The only [[Legendary Pokémon]] included in the set is {{p|Giratina}}, which is included twice ({{TCG ID|Platinum|Giratina|28}} and {{TCG ID|Platinum|Giratina LV.X|124}}).

