'''Scarlet & Violet: Arcane Truth''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 真实玄虚''') is the sixth {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet era.

== Information ==
'''Arcane Truth''' is the sixth Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. Most of its cards originate from the Japanese {{TCG|Ancient Roar}} and {{TCG|Future Flash}} sets, introducing the {{TCG|Ancient}} and {{TCG|Future}} cards from those sets. The expansion focuses on {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Iron Valiant ex|89}}, the {{ct|Psychic}} {{DL|Pokémon ex (TCG)|Tera Pokémon ex}}, which was also the focus of the Japanese {{TCG|Future Flash}} and English {{TCG|Paradox Rift}} expansions.

Arcane Truth features two cards exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language: a {{TCG|special illustration rare}} print of [[Iron Hands ex (Paradox Rift 70)|Iron Hands ex]], and a {{TCG|hyper rare}} print of [[Pal Pad (Flashfire 92)|Pal Pad]].

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 128 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and a rarer one with a Master Ball motif.

