'''Scarlet & Violet: Ardent Obsidian''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 黑晶炽诚''') is the fifth {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet era.

== Information ==
[[File:CSV5 banner.png|thumb|300px|Set banner artwork]]
'''Ardent Obsidian''' is the fifth Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. Most of its cards originate from the Japanese {{TCG|Ruler of the Black Flame}}, {{TCG|Raging Surf}}, {{TCG|Ancient Roar}}, and {{TCG|Future Flash}} sets, though no {{TCG|Ancient}} or {{TCG|Future}} cards from the latter two sets are included. The expansion focuses on {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Charizard ex|125}}, the {{ct|Darkness}} {{DL|Pokémon ex (TCG)|Tera Pokémon ex}}, which was also the focus of the Japanese {{TCG|Ruler of the Black Flame}} and English {{TCG|Obsidian Flames}} expansions.

Ardent Obsidian features two cards exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language: a {{TCG|special illustration rare}} print of {{TCG|Larry}}, and a {{TCG|hyper rare}} print of {{TCG|Defiance Band}}.

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 115 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and a rarer one with a Master Ball motif.

