'''Aura Seeker''' (Japanese: '''ハドウシーカー''' ''Aura Seeker'') is the name given to the seventh expansion of cards released during the Japanese [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s MEGA Series. This set introduces Z [[Mega Evolution]] Pokémon into the Trading Card Game, first introduced in the [[Mega Dimension]] DLC of the video game {{g|Legends: Z-A}}.

==Information==
'''Aura Seeker''' introduces cards featuring Z [[Mega Evolution]] Pokémon, a concept which was first revealed in the [[Mega Dimension]] DLC of the video game {{g|Legends: Z-A}}, as {{TCG|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}}. Mechanically, Mega Evolution Pokémon ex cards featuring Z Mega Evolution do not differ from regular Mega Evolution Pokémon ex cards. Cards in this expansion were first revealed at the conclusion of the [[2026 Pokémon World Championships]] in San Francisco, California, United States.

The title "Aura Seeker" was known from a trademark filed by [[The Pokémon Company]] on March 2, 2026.<ref>[https://www.j-platpat.inpit.go.jp/c1801/TR/JP-2026-021914/40/en Trademark Appl.No.2026-21914] — J-PlatPat (Japan Platform for Patent Information)</ref> Cards released in this set are included in the English "{{TCG|FLO}}" expansion.

Aura Seeker will be released in {{pmin|Japan}} on November 27, 2026<!--, followed by localized releases in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}} on XXXXX, 2026, and in {{pmin|South Korea}} on XXXXX, 2026--> . Each booster pack contains 5 cards. Each booster box contains 30 packs.

