'''Black Bolt''' (Japanese: '''ブラックボルト''') and '''White Flare''' (Japanese: '''ホワイトフレア''') are the names given to the two Japanese paired sets that collectively make up the eleventh and final expansion of cards released during the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s Scarlet & Violet Era. These sets feature [[Generation V]] and the [[Unova]] region.

==Information==
'''Black Bolt''' and '''White Flare''' are paired sets which are primarily based on [[Generation V]], with cards featuring all 156 Pokémon originally introduced in the [[Unova]] region. Every single Pokémon card introduced in this expansion has a secret rare variant of AR ({{TCG|Illustration rare|Art Rare}}) or better. Tinsel Holofoil cards are also reintroduced with the release of these sets. In contrast to the original {{TCG|Black & White|Black Collection and White Collection}} and [[Pokémon Black & White Versions|the games that they were based on]], Black Bolt and White Flare each center around the [[version mascot]] matching their color; thus, Black Bolt is themed around {{p|Zekrom}}, while White Flare is themed around {{p|Reshiram}}.

Black Bolt and White Flare also introduces a new rarity of cards called '''BWR''' (BW Rare), also known as '''Black White rare''' in the English release, which feature Pokémon against a stark solid color background with monochromatic card designs and elaborate Holofoil patterning. The only two cards introduced that have the BWR rarity are {{TCG ID|Black Bolt|Zekrom ex|174}} and {{TCG ID|White Flare|Reshiram ex|174}} from their respective sets.

Black Bolt and White Flare were released in Japan on June 6, 2025. Each booster box contains 20 {{TCG|booster pack}}s. There are two kinds of booster packs for each set that are available for purchase: regular packs cost ¥290 and contain 7 cards, with 2 cards guaranteed to be Holofoil, while "Deluxe Packs" cost ¥1450 and contain 35 cards, with 1 card guaranteed to have a [[rarity]] of AR or better. Releasing on the same day in Japan is the '''Black Bolt / White Flare Card File Set''' (Japanese: '''ブラックボルト・ホワイトフレア カードファイルセット'''), which contains a 3-pocket card file album that can store up to 156 cards, a promo card of Victini, and 3 booster packs of Black Bolt and White Flare each.

Black Bolt and White Flare are also released in {{pmin|Chinese|Traditional Chinese}} on June 20, 2025, and in {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} on August 1, 2025. A Collector's Set featuring a {{TCTCG|SV-P Promotional cards|SV-P Promotional card}} of {{TCG ID|SV-P Promo|Zorua|241}} is also released in Traditional Chinese on the same day.

