'''Scarlet & Violet: Blade Awakening''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 利刃猛醒''') is the seventh {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet Series.<ref name="SC19812"/>

== Information ==
'''Blade Awakening''' is the seventh Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. Most of its cards originate from the Japanese {{TCG|Wild Force}}, {{TCG|Cyber Judge}}, and {{TCG|Crimson Haze}} sets, as well as a small number from other sets and products, including {{TCG|Transformation Mask}}, the {{TCG|Starter Deck & Build Sets}}, and the {{TCG|Generations Start Decks}}. The expansion focuses on {{OBP|Greninja ex|Twilight Masquerade 106}}, the {{ct|Fighting}} {{DL|Pokémon ex (TCG)|Tera Pokémon ex}}, and sees the introduction of {{TCG|ACE SPEC}} cards to the Simplified Chinese language version of the game.

Blade Awakening features one card exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language: a {{TCG|special illustration rare}} print of {{TCG|Ciphermaniac's Codebreaking}}.

In total, excluding the aforementioned exclusive card, the set's cards originate from the following Japanese releases:
* 85 cards from {{TCG|Cyber Judge}};
* 83 cards from {{TCG|Wild Force}};
* 53 cards from {{TCG|Crimson Haze}};
* 15 cards from {{TCG|Transformation Mask}};
* 9 cards from the {{TCG|Generations Start Decks}};
* 6 cards from the {{TCG|Starter Deck & Build Sets}};
* 4 cards from {{TCG|Stellar Miracle}};
* 1 card each from {{TCG|Night Wanderer}}, {{TCG|Paradise Dragona}}, and {{TCG|Super Electric Breaker}}.

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 173 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and a rarer one with a Master Ball motif.

=== Iron Thorns printing error ===
On December 25, 2025, the official Pokémon website for Mainland China announced that the {{OBP|Iron Thorns|Temporal Forces 62}} card's Megaton Lariat attack had been misspelled on the rare print, being spelled as 百万吨金勾臂 (the Traditional Chinese spelling) instead of 百万吨金钩臂 (the Simplified Chinese spelling). The art rare print features the correct spelling. This does not affect the playability of either print or their eligibility in official matches.<ref name="IronThorns"/>

