'''Scarlet & Violet: Bonus Round''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 嘉奖回合''') is the fourth {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet Series.

== Information ==
[[File:CSV4 banner.png|thumb|300px|Set banner artwork]]
'''Bonus Round''' is the fourth Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. While many of its cards originate from the Japanese {{TCG|ex Start Decks}} and the {{TCG|Ruler of the Black Flame}}, {{TCG|Ancient Roar}}, and {{TCG|Future Flash}} sets, it also includes a number of cards from earlier sets and promotional products. The expansion focuses primarily on {{OBP|Gholdengo ex|Bonus Round 144}}, the Coin Entity Pokémon, which was also one of the focuses of the Japanese {{TCG|Raging Surf}} subset.

Bonus Round features three cards exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language: a {{TCG|hyper rare}} print of {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Gholdengo ex|139}} and {{TCG|special illustration rare}} prints of {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Maushold ex|155}} and {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Rika|172}}.

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 129 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and one with a rarer Master Ball motif.
