'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—151''''' is the first special expansion released during the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released on September 22, 2023. 

==Blurb==
<i>[[Gotta catch 'em all!|Gotta Catch ’Em All!]]

Team up with Bulbasaur, Charmander, and Squirtle, and witness a brand-new dawn in Kanto! With this new day comes a new chance to track down old friends, make new partners, and capture every last one of the original 151. Discover the extraordinary Venusaur ex, Charizard ex, and Blastoise ex in special cards with captivating illustrations, and explore the cities and countryside of a reinvigorated land—you might even find the elusive Mew ex in your travels. New adventures will unfold and new horizons will be revealed in the Scarlet & Violet—151 expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Scarlet & Violet—151''' is a special expansion that includes only [[Generation I]] Pokémon. Unlike in most expansions, Pokémon cards in this expansion are ordered according to the Pokémon's [[List of Pokémon by National Pokédex number|National Pokédex numbers]] instead of being grouped by their types.<ref>[https://www.pokemon.com/us/pokemon-tcg/scarlet-violet-151/explore-and-watch/ Scarlet & Violet—151] — Pokemon.com</ref> Like other special expansions, such as {{TCG|Crown Zenith}}, individual 151 booster packs cannot be purchased separately and are instead available exclusively in various set-related products.

The [[Kanto first partner Pokémon]] and their first Evolutions are featured on illustration rare cards, while their final Evolutions are featured as {{TCG|Pokémon ex}}. [[Bill]], [[Daisy Oak]], [[Erika]], and [[Giovanni]], all of whom are characters from the [[Kanto]] region, are present on {{TCG|Supporter card}}s. Additionally, the Evolution Pokémon cards and their corresponding Basic Pokémon are each illustrated by the same illustrator. This also applies to the illustration rare and special illustration rare cards of the first partner Pokémon and their Evolutions.

For the first time since the [[Platinum: Arceus (TCG)|Arceus]] expansion, the [[Fossil]] Pokémon {{TCG ID|151|Omanyte|138}}, {{TCG ID|151|Kabuto|140}}, and {{TCG ID|151|Aerodactyl|142}} are able to evolve directly from a corresponding {{DL|Fossil|Fossil Trainer card}} instead of from {{TCG ID|Ultra Prism|Unidentified Fossil|134}}. The Fossil Trainer cards corresponding to Omanyte, Kabuto, and Aerodactyl are {{TCG ID|151|Antique Helix Fossil|153}}, {{TCG ID|151|Antique Dome Fossil|152}}, and {{TCG ID|151|Antique Old Amber|154}}, respectively. This subset is also notable for introducing the first {{TCG|Kadabra}} card since the release of {{TCG ID|Skyridge|Kadabra|69}} from the {{TCG|Skyridge}} expansion in 2003, 20 years prior.

151 includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Pokémon Card 151}} expansion. This expansion contains 12 {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} cards, 16 {{TCG|illustration rare}} cards, 16 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon and Supporter cards, seven {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards. The illustration rare prints of {{TCG ID|Pokémon Card 151|Snorlax|181}} and {{TCG ID|Pokémon Card 151|Mewtwo|183}} from Pokémon Card 151 were released as {{TCG|SVP Black Star Promos}} in the {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|151 Elite Trainer Box}} and the {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|151 Ultra-Premium Collection}}, respectively; the 151 Ultra-Premium Collection also included the special illustration rare print of {{TCG ID|Pokémon Card 151|Mew ex|205}} from that set.

Cosmos Holofoil {{TCG|SVE Basic Energies|Basic Energy cards}} can also be found in 151 booster packs. There is also a low probability to find an entire evolutionary line of Bulbasaur, Charmander, or Squirtle as secret cards in the same booster pack, in place of the two Reverse Holo cards and the Rare card. Fans refer to such packs as "demigod packs."<ref>[https://thepokecourt.com/blogs/resources/english-booster-box-guaranteed-hit-rates-god-packs Modern English "God" and "Demigod" Packs | The Poke Court]</ref>

