'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Paldea Evolved''''' is the second main expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released on June 9, 2023.

==Blurb==
<i>Command a Rousing Performance!

Energy surges as new powers awaken and perilous legends are revealed! First partners Meowscarada ex, Skeledirge ex, and Quaquaval ex have evolved to take the stage with mesmerizing magic, song, and dance. Meanwhile, Forretress, Slowking, and Dedenne shine as Tera Pokémon ex, and Chien-Pao ex, Ting-Lu ex, and others bring daunting strengths requiring courage to command. Even Pikachu joins the Pokémon ex party in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Paldea Evolved expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Paldea Evolved''' features the three final [[Evolution]]s of the [[Paldea]]n [[first partner Pokémon]], {{p|Meowscarada}}, {{p|Skeledirge}}, and {{p|Quaquaval}}, as well as the [[treasures of ruin]]. The set continues to debut Pokémon and characters from the {{g|Scarlet and Violet}} [[Pokémon games]], with various locations in the [[Paldea]] [[region]] depicted in the illustrations.

{{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Baxcalibur|60}}'s Super Cold {{TCG|Ability}} allows multiple {{TCG|Basic Water Energy}} to be attached per turn, which synergizes with {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Chien-Pao ex|61}}'s Shivery Chill Ability to strengthen its Hail Blade attack; these Energy cards can then be retrieved with {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Super Rod|188}} and {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Superior Energy Retrieval|189}}. {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Wigglytuff|84}} can use its Balloon Therapy Ability to attach an additional {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Therapeutic Energy|193}} during a player's turn; this can be attached to {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Slaking|162}} to allow it to attack consistently without becoming {{TCG|Asleep}}. {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Copperajah ex|150}} can use its Nosequake attack to damage the player's own Benched Pokémon, which can allow any of the set's {{dl|Tauros (TCG)|Paldean Tauros}} cards to deal more damage with their {{cw|Raging Horns}} attack; additionally, the {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Bravery Charm|173}} can be attached to Paldean Tauros to further increase its capacity to take damage, allowing Raging Horns to inflict even more damage. This set also debuts Pokémon with the {{cw|United Wings}} attack in {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Wattrel|80}}, {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Murkrow|131}}, and {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Flamigo|170}}, which can deal more damage with United Wings for each other Pokémon with the same attack in the player's discard pile.

The set contains 14 {{TCG|Pokémon ex}}, three Tera Pokémon ex, 36 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, 18 {{TCG|ultra rare}} Pokémon ex, 8 ultra rare Supporter cards, 15 {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards and 9 {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Paldea Evolved includes cards from the Japanese expansions {{TCG|Triplet Beat}}, {{TCG|Snow Hazard}}, and {{TCG|Clay Burst}}, although some cards were not localized until the release of the following {{TCG|Obsidian Flames}} expansion. Cards from the {{TCG|ex Starter Set Pikachu ex & Pawmot}} Standard Deck and the {{TCG|Premium Trainer Box ex}} are also included in Paldea Evolved.

