'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Paradox Rift''''' is the fourth expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released on November 3, 2023.

==Blurb==
<i>Uncover the Anomalies of Area Zero!

Dive into the clouds and explore a land that appears to be unbound by time! With ferocious attacks, Ancient Pokémon like Roaring Moon ex and Sandy Shocks ex appear alongside artificial Future Pokémon like Iron Valiant ex and Iron Hands ex. Meanwhile, Garchomp ex, Mewtwo ex, and others Terastallize to gain new types, as Armarouge ex, Gholdengo ex, and more Pokémon ex join the fray. Adventure awaits as timelines collide in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Paradox Rift expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Paradox Rift''' features [[Paradox Pokémon]]. Although the {{p|Koraidon}}, {{p|Miraidon}}, {{p|Great Tusk}}, and {{p|Iron Treads}} appeared in the {{TCG|Scarlet & Violet}} expansion, Paradox Rift features Paradox Pokémon that do not appear outside of [[Area Zero]] in the [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]] video games. Card illustrations from these sets depict Pokémon within and around Area Zero.

The set was first previewed on August 11, 2023, when the Canadian Pokémon Center website briefly showed off one of the Elite Trainer Boxes for the set featuring {{p|Iron Valiant}}.{{fact}} More information about the set was revealed during the closing ceremony of the [[2023 Pokémon World Championships]] on August 13, 2023.<ref>[https://press.pokemon.com/en/MEDIA-ALERT-New-Pokemon-Trading-Card-Game-Scarlet-VioletParadox-Rift-E MEDIA ALERT: New Pokémon Trading Card Game: ''Scarlet & Violet—Paradox Rift'' Expansion Introduces Ancient and Future Pokémon | The Pokémon Company North America Official Press Site]</ref>

Two new variants of cards are introduced in this expansion: '''{{TCG|Ancient}}''' and '''{{TCG|Future}}''', which are both available as Pokémon and Trainer cards. Both card variants feature unique text icons on the top right corner of the artwork, and unique backgrounds adorning the right half of the cards: Ancient cards have a layered {{wp|Stratum|strata}} background, while Future cards have a pixelated background. Ancient Pokémon cards tend to have direct attacks that deal a large amount of damage and are difficult to Knock Out. Future Pokémon cards tend to have {{TCG|Ability|Abilities}} and attacks with extra effects, allowing for craftier strategies. {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Ancient Booster Energy Capsule|159}} can bolster Ancient Pokémon defensively and enable {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Brute Bonnet|123}}'s Ability, while {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Future Booster Energy Capsule|164}} can empower Future Pokémon's attacks and reduce the cost of {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Iron Jugulis|216}}'s second attack.

Additional strategies are available to other Pokémon in the set. {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Tsareena ex|46}} can add damage counters to an opponent's Pokémon and reduce their remaining HP below 30, which prevents that Pokémon from attacking while {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Vanilluxe|45}} is in play. The [[treasures of ruin]] {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Wo-Chien|18}}, {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Chi-Yu|29}}, {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Chien-Pao|57}}, and {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Ting-Lu|109}} each have attacks that can each accelerate Energy from the discard pile to the player's Benched Pokémon. {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Simisage|5}}, {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Simisear|21}}, and {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Simipour|42}} each have the {{cw|Monkey Trio}} Ability, which reduces their attack costs while all three are in play. Paradox Rift also includes {{TCG|Technical Machine card}}s, first reintroduced in the Japanese {{TCG|Raging Surf}} subset after being last seen in the {{TCG|Rising Rivals}} expansion. Technical Machine cards as of this set are categorized as {{TCG|Pokémon Tool card}}s.

Paradox Rift includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Ancient Roar}} and {{TCG|Future Flash}} expansions, the {{TCG|Raging Surf}} subset, and the {{TCG|Terastal Starter Sets}}. The Hyper rare prints of {{TCG|Basic Darkness Energy}} and {{TCG|Basic Metal Energy}} from Ancient Roar and Future Flash respectively are instead included in {{TCG|Shrouded Fable}}. Other cards from these sets not included in Paradox Rift are included in the {{TCG|Paldean Fates}} expansion. Paradox Rift contains 13 {{TCG|Pokémon ex}}, seven Tera Pokémon ex, 34 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, 15 {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, 28 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, and seven {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Paradox Rift is available in English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, and Portuguese.

