'''Ruler of the Black Flame''' (Japanese: '''{{ruby|黒|こく}}{{ruby|炎|えん}}の{{ruby|支|し}}{{ruby|配|はい}}{{ruby|者|しゃ}}''')  is the name given to the third Japanese expansion of cards released during the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s {{TCG|Scarlet & Violet Era}}.

==Information==
'''Ruler of the Black Flame''' is the first set to feature Tera {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} with {{TCG|type}}s that differ from their usual types. Type-shifted Tera Pokémon ex use the same Energy types as their usual type for their attacks, but have differing Weakness and Resistance in accordance with their shifted type. Other cards from this set depict [[Pokémon Center]]s in the [[Paldea]] [[region]] in the illustrations' backgrounds.

Cards released in this expansion reference other cards previously released in the {{dl|List of Japanese Pokémon Trading Card Game expansions|PCG Era}}. {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Charizard ex|125}}, like {{TCG ID|Offense and Defense of the Furthest Ends|Charizard ☆ δ |52}} from the {{TCG|Offense and Defense of the Furthest Ends}} expansion, has the {{TCG|Darkness}} type, and {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Tyranitar ex|66}} has the {{TCG|Lightning}} type like {{TCG ID|Shockwave! Tyranitar Deck|Tyranitar ex δ|4}} from the {{TCG|Shockwave! Tyranitar ex Constructed Standard Deck}}. Additionally, {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Pidgeot ex|164}} features the Quick Search {{TCG|Ability}}, which first appeared as a {{TCG|Poké-Power}} on {{TCG ID|Flight of Legends|Pidgeot|64}} from the {{TCG|Flight of Legends}} expansion.

This is also the first expansion since the {{dl|List of Japanese Pokémon Trading Card Game expansions|Sun & Moon Era}} to feature [[Baby Pokémon]] that do not evolve into {{TCG|Stage 1 Pokémon}}, as it includes {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Cleffa|80}} and {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Bonsly|110}}. These cards have each an attack with no Energy and no [[retreat cost]], like those from the {{dl|List of Japanese Pokémon Trading Card Game expansions|LEGEND Era}}, although unlike previous cards featuring Baby Pokémon, these have Weakness.

The set's Charizard ex can use its Ability to attach {{TCG|Basic Fire Energy}} cards from the player's deck upon Evolution, which can be used to strengthen {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Entei|30}}'s Blaze Ball attack. Another strategy is to use {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Town Store|196}} to find {{TCG|Pokémon Tool card}}s to attach to {{TCG ID|Obsidian Flames|Revavroom ex|156}}, which can have up to four attached simultaneously because of its Ability.

Ruler of the Black Flame contains four Pokémon ex, four Tera Pokémon ex, 12 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, six {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, 12 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Ruler of the Black Flame was released in Japanese on July 28, 2023, followed by localized releases in Traditional Chinese on August 11, 2023, in Korean on August 25, 2023, and in Thai on September 29, 2023. The Indonesian set equivalent, {{ATCG|Black Shine}}, released much later on October 27, 2023.

Cards released in this set are included in the English {{TCG|Obsidian Flames}} expansion.

