'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Shrouded Fable''''' is the third special expansion released during the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released on August 2, 2024.

==Blurb==
<i>Shadowy Secrets & Toxic Tricks!

Rumors swirl and memories deceive as the march of time beats on in the land of Kitakami! Prepare for nightfall and discover a malevolent presence as Pecharunt ex commands the Loyal Three—Okidogi ex, Munkidori ex, and Fezandipiti ex—to do its nefarious bidding. Meanwhile, Revavroom ex plugs into the grid to Terastallize into a Lightning type, and Kingdra ex makes a royal splash in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Shrouded Fable expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Shrouded Fable''' introduces the [[Mythical Pokémon]] {{p|Pecharunt}}, who first appeared in the [[Mochi Mayhem]] epilogue of [[The Hidden Treasure of Area Zero]] DLC for [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]], as a {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} card. The [[Loyal Three]], a group of [[Legendary Pokémon]] associated with Pecharunt, also appear in this expansion as Pokémon ex cards after their debut in the {{TCG|Twilight Masquerade}} expansion. The set additionally features {{type|Dark}} and {{type|Poison}} Pokémon and characters associated with [[villainous team]]s, including [[Cassiopeia]], [[Colress]], and [[Xerosic]].

Additionally, Shrouded Fable introduces a new unique Holofoil pattern to Pokémon Trading Card Game cards known as "parallel foil." Like other types of Reverse Holofoil cards, parallel foil cards can be distinguished by the white expansion code box with black text, in contrast to regular cards, which have black expansion code boxes with white text.

Some cards in Shrouded Fable have effects focused on making the player's own Active Pokémon {{TCG|Poisoned}}. {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Pecharunt ex|39}} can switch {{ct|Darkness}} Pokémon to the Active Spot and make them Poisoned while {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Janine's Secret Art|59}} can attach additional Energy to Darkness-type Pokémon while making them Poisoned. These effects can be combined with {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Binding Mochi|55}}, which increases damage dealt by Poisoned Pokémon, and with {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Okidogi ex|36}}, which can become Poisoned from its first attack to deal increased damage with its second attack. {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Munkidori ex|37}} can also synergize with Pecharunt ex, as Munkidori ex's {{TCG|Ability}} reduces the Prize cards opponents take when it is Knocked Out if Pecharunt ex is in play. Additionally, the Pokémon {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Crobat|29}}, {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Malamar|34}}, and {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Kyurem|47}} have effects that interact with the {{TCG|Supporter card}}s Janine's Secret Art, {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Xerosic's Machinations|64}}, and {{TCG ID|Shrouded Fable|Colress's Tenacity|57}}, respectively.

Shrouded Fable includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Night Wanderer}} expansion. The illustration rare prints of {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Munkidori|107}}, {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Fezandipiti|108}}, and {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Okidogi|110}} from the Japanese {{TCG|Transformation Mask}} expansion are also included in this set instead of in {{TCG|Twilight Masquerade}}. Additionally, the Hyper rare prints of {{TCG|Basic Darkness Energy}} and {{TCG|Basic Metal Energy}} from the Japanese {{TCG|Ancient Roar}} and {{TCG|Future Flash}} expansions respectively are included in this set instead of in {{TCG|Paradox Rift}}.

Shrouded Fable contains three {{TCG|ACE SPEC card|ACE SPEC}} Trainer cards (including the first ever {{TCG|ACE SPEC card|ACE SPEC}} {{TCG|Stadium card}}); five {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} and one Tera Pokémon ex; 15 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon; 10 {{TCG|ultra rare}} Pokémon ex, Tera Pokémon ex and Supporter cards; five {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards; and five {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Shrouded Fable is available in English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, and Portuguese.

