'''Snow Hazard''' (Japanese: '''スノーハザード''') and '''Clay Burst''' and (Japanese: '''クレイバースト''') are the names given to the two Japanese paired sets that collectively make up the second main expansion of cards released during the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s {{TCG|Scarlet & Violet Era}}.

==Information==
'''Snow Hazard''' and  '''Clay Burst''' feature {{p|Chien-Pao}}, {{p|Ting-Lu}}, and the other [[treasures of ruin]] from the [[Paldea]] [[region]] as powerful Pokémon ex cards. These sets continue to debut Pokémon and characters from the {{g|Scarlet and Violet}} [[Pokémon games]], with various locations in the [[Paldea]] [[region]] depicted in the illustrations.

Snow Hazard features the {{ct|Water}} Pokémon {{p|Chien-Pao}} while Clay Burst features the {{ct|Fighting}} Pokémon {{p|Ting-Lu}}. No {{ct|Fire}} or {{ct|Lightning}} Pokémon are included in Snow Hazard; likewise, no Water-type or {{ct|Metal}} Pokémon are included in Clay Burst.

From the Snow Hazard set, {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Baxcalibur|60}}'s Super Cold {{TCG|Ability}} allows multiple {{TCG|Basic Water Energy}} to be attached per turn, which synergizes with {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Chien-Pao ex|61}}'s Shivery Chill Ability to strengthen its Hail Blade attack; these Energy cards can then be shuffled back into the deck with {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Super Rod|188}}. Clay Burst's {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Wigglytuff|84}} can use its Balloon Therapy Ability to attach an additional {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Therapeutic Energy|193}}, also from Clay Burst, during a player's turn; this can be attached to {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Slaking|162}} from Snow Hazard to allow it to attack consistently without becoming {{TCG|Asleep}}. These sets also add new Pokémon that have the {{cw|United Wings}} attack, with {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Murkrow|131}} in Snow Hazard and {{TCG ID|Paldea Evolved|Flamigo|170}} in Clay Burst, which can deal more damage with United Wings for each other Pokémon with the same attack in the player's discard pile.

Each set contains five {{TCG|Pokémon ex}}, one Tera Pokémon ex, 12 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, eight {{TCG|ultra rare}} Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, five {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Snow Hazard and Clay Burst were released in Japan on April 14, 2023, followed by localized releases in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}} on April 28, 2023, in {{pmin|Indonesia}} on June 2, 2023, in {{pmin|South Korea}} on June 14, 2023, and in {{pmin|Thailand}} on June 30, 2023.

Cards released in these sets were included primarily in the English {{TCG|Paldea Evolved}} expansion, though some were not localized until the release of the following {{TCG|Obsidian Flames}} expansion.

