'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Stellar Crown''''' is the seventh main expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released on September 13, 2024.

==Blurb==
<i>An Adventure to Awaken the Power Within!

Descend into a world below the surface and discover the true potential of the Terastal phenomenon! The Legendary Pokémon Terapagos takes the throne, joined by Cinderace ex, Lapras ex, and Galvantula ex, all wielding brilliant new powers as Stellar Tera Pokémon ex. The newly discovered Hydrapple ex leads even more Pokémon ex into battle, and ACE SPEC cards continue to shake up the game in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Stellar Crown expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Stellar Crown''' focuses on {{Tera}} or {{Tera}}stallized Pokémon, with {{p|Terapagos}} as the main featured Pokémon, as well as various other Pokémon, characters and settings associated with [[The Indigo Disk]], the second part of [[The Hidden Treasure of Area Zero]] DLC for the [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]] video games. These include newly-introduced [[Paradox Pokémon]] in {{p|Raging Bolt}} and {{p|Iron Boulder}}, newly-introduced [[List of cross-generational evolutionary lines|cross-generational Evolutions]] in {{p|Hydrapple}} and {{p|Archaludon}}, and returning Evolutions of [[first partner Pokémon]] in {{p|Venusaur}}, {{p|Blastoise}}, and {{p|Greninja}}, as well as the characters [[Briar]], [[Crispin]], and [[Lacey]].

As the set's name implies, Stellar Crown debuts Terastallized {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} with the {{t|Stellar}} type for the first time in the TCG, known as '''Stellar Tera Pokémon ex'''. Cards of Stellar Tera Pokémon ex have several unique distinctions: they all have TCG {{TCG|type}}s that follow the Pokémon's usual typing, as well as a uniquely powerful attack that is named after gemstones and requires three different types of Energy to use. To support these Pokémon, this set also introduces {{TCG|Trainer card}}s which ease these Energy requirements in {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Glass Trumpet|135}} and {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Crispin|133}}, which let the player attach extra Energy during their turn.

{{cat|Cards that reference Tera Pokémon}} enable strong support effects while these Pokémon are in play: these include {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Sparkling Crystal|142}}, which reduces the Energy requirements for attacks used by Tera Pokémon; {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Noctowl|115}}, which allows the player to search their deck for Trainer cards; {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Area Zero Underdepths|131}}, which allows players to add more Pokémon to their Bench; and {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Briar|132}}, which allows the player to take an extra Prize card when Knocking Out their opponent's Pokémon with a Tera Pokémon. {{ct|Colorless}} Pokémon that can enable {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Terapagos ex|128}} are also present, as {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Bouffalant|119}} can reduce damage taken by Colorless Pokémon and {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Fan Rotom|118}} can search the deck for other Colorless Pokémon, including Noctowl and Bouffalant.

Stellar Crown includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Stellar Miracle}} expansion and the {{TCG|Pokémon Card Game Battle Academy}} Deck Kit. The set also includes reprints of cards from the {{TCG|151}} expansion with new art, including {{TCG ID|Special Deck Set ex|Venusaur ex|3}}, {{TCG ID|Special Deck Set ex|Blastoise ex|16}}, and illustration rare prints of {{TCG ID|Special Deck Set ex|Bulbasaur|50}} and {{TCG ID|Special Deck Set ex|Squirtle|52}}, which were originally included in the Japanese {{TCG|Venusaur & Charizard & Blastoise Special Deck Set ex}}. Instead of appearing in Stellar Crown, the illustration rare print of {{TCG ID|Stellar Miracle|Noctowl|114}} from Stellar Miracle was made available as a {{TCG|SVP Black Star Promos|SVP Black Star Promotional}} card in the {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|Stellar Crown Elite Trainer Box}}, while the ultra rare print of {{TCG ID|Stellar Miracle|Terapagos ex|122}} from Stellar Miracle instead released as a Black Star Promo in the {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|Terapagos ex Ultra-Premium Collection}}.

Stellar Crown contains three {{TCG|ACE SPEC card|ACE SPEC}} Trainer cards, 10 Pokémon ex, four Stellar Tera Pokémon ex, 13 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, 11 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, six {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Stellar Crown is available in English, German, French, Italian, Spanish and Portuguese.

