'''Stellar Miracle''' (Japanese: '''ステラミラクル''') is the name given to the seventh Japanese expansion of cards released during the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s Scarlet & Violet Era.

==Information==
'''Stellar Miracle''' focuses on {{Tera}} or {{Tera}}stallized Pokémon, with {{p|Terapagos}} as the main featured Pokémon, as well as various other Pokémon, characters and settings associated with [[The Indigo Disk]], the second part of [[The Hidden Treasure of Area Zero]] DLC for the [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]] video games. These include newly-introduced [[Paradox Pokémon]] in {{p|Raging Bolt}} and {{p|Iron Boulder}} and newly-introduced [[List of cross-generational evolutionary lines|cross-generational Evolutions]] in {{p|Hydrapple}} and {{p|Archaludon}}, as well as the characters [[Briar]], [[Crispin]], and [[Lacey]].

As the set's name implies, Stellar Crown debuts Terastallized {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} with the {{t|Stellar}} type for the first time in the TCG, known as '''Stellar Tera Pokémon ex'''. Cards of Stellar Tera Pokémon ex have several unique distinctions: they all have TCG {{TCG|type}}s that follow the Pokémon's usual typing, as well as a uniquely powerful attack that is named after gemstones and requires three different types of Energy to use. To support these Pokémon, this set also introduces [[Trainer cards (TCG)|Trainer cards]] which ease these Energy requirements in {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Glass Trumpet|135}} and {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Crispin|133}}, which let the player attach extra Energy during their turn.

{{cat|Cards that reference Tera Pokémon}} enable strong support effects while these Pokémon are in play: these include {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Sparkling Crystal|142}}, which reduces the Energy requirements for attacks used by Tera Pokémon; {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Noctowl|115}}, which allows the player to search their deck for Trainer cards; {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Area Zero Underdepths|131}}, which allows players to add more Pokémon to their Bench; and {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Briar|132}}, which allows the player to take an extra Prize card when Knocking Out their opponent's Pokémon with a Tera Pokémon. {{ct|Colorless}} Pokémon that can enable {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Terapagos ex|128}} are also present, as {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Bouffalant|119}} can reduce damage taken by Colorless Pokémon while {{TCG ID|Stellar Crown|Fan Rotom|118}} can search the deck for other Colorless Pokémon, including Noctowl and Bouffalant.

Stellar Miracle contains three {{TCG|ACE SPEC card|ACE SPEC}} Trainer cards, four Pokémon ex, four Stellar Tera Pokémon ex, 12 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, 12 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, six {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Stellar Miracle was released in Japanese on July 19, 2024, followed by localized releases in Traditional Chinese on August 2, 2024<!-- and in Korean on ??-->. The Thai and Indonesian set equivalent, {{ATCG|Stellar Guidance}}, was released on August 30, 2024 and September 20, 2024 in the respective regions. The release of Stellar Miracle in Japanese was accompanied by the release of the {{TCG|Stellar Miracle Deck Build Box}}, while the Traditional Chinese release was accompanied with the releases of the '''Pokémon Horizons: The Series Special Card Set''' (Traditional Chinese: '''特別卡組 寶可夢地平線：系列''' ''Special Card Set Pokémon Horizons: The Series''), which includes 10 booster packs of Stellar Miracle and 3 promo cards featuring characters from ''[[Pokémon Horizons: The Series]]''; and the '''Stellar Miracle Collector's Set''' (Traditional Chinese: '''星晶奇跡 收藏家組合''' ''Star Crystal Miracle Collector's Set''), a product similar to the Collector's Set of the previous {{TCG|Transformation Mask}} expansion, which features 10 booster packs, a card list booklet and a Full Art promo card of {{TCG ID|SV-P Promo|Zeraora|133}}.

Cards released in this set are included in the English {{TCG|Stellar Crown}} expansion. The illustration rare print of {{TCG ID|Stellar Miracle|Noctowl|114}} and ultra rare print of {{TCG ID|Stellar Miracle|Terapagos ex|122}} from Stellar Miracle are not present in Stellar Crown, instead released as {{TCG|SVP Black Star Promos|SVP Black Star Promotional}} cards in the {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|Stellar Crown Elite Trainer Box}} and {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|Terapagos ex Ultra-Premium Collection}}, respectively.

