'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Temporal Forces''''' is the fifth main expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released on March 22, 2024.

==Blurb==
<i>Ancient & Future Powers Endure!

The ranks of Ancient and Future Pokémon continue to grow! Walking Wake ex breaks free of the past alongside Raging Bolt ex, while Iron Leaves ex delivers high-tech justice with Iron Crown ex. Outside Area Zero, Wugtrio and Farigiraf shift types as Tera Pokémon ex, and Pokémon Trainers everywhere prepare for the return of ACE SPEC cards with uniquely powerful effects. A rupture in time brings wild beasts and cyber visions to battle in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Temporal Forces expansion!</i>

==Information==
The '''Temporal Forces''' set continues to introduce {{TCG|Ancient}} and {{TCG|Future}} Pokémon and Trainer cards into the Pokémon Trading Card Game. The central Pokémon in this set are {{p|Koraidon}}, {{p|Miraidon}}, and the trios of [[Paradox Pokémon]] resembling the [[Legendary beasts]] and the [[Swords of Justice]]: {{p|Walking Wake}}, {{p|Gouging Fire}}, {{p|Raging Bolt}}, {{p|Iron Leaves}}, {{p|Iron Boulder}}, and {{p|Iron Crown}}.

These sets also reintroduced {{TCG|ACE SPEC card}}s. First introduced in the Black & White Series of the TCG, ACE SPEC cards are powerful cards with the restriction that only one ACE SPEC card of any sort can be included in a deck. ACE SPEC cards as of this set have a unique magenta design and may be {{TCG|Trainer card}}s or {{TCG|Special Energy card}}s.

Playing multiple Ancient Pokémon together increases the damage {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Koraidon|119}} can deal and allows more cards to be drawn with the ACE SPEC {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Awakening Drum|141}}. Using the {{TCG|Supporter card}} {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Explorer's Guidance|147}} allows {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Great Tusk|97}} to discard more cards from the opponent's deck, while {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Roaring Moon|109}} can deal more damage with more Ancient cards in the player's discard pile. These Pokémon can also increase their defensive capability using the {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Ancient Booster Energy Capsule|159}}, which has been reprinted in this set. Additionally, {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Scream Tail|77}} can be played to heal damage from Ancient Pokémon on the Bench. The Future Pokémon can deal more damage while {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Crown ex|81}} is in play, and additional Energy can be attached to them using {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Miraidon|121}} and the ACE SPEC {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Reboot Pod|158}}. Playing the Supporter card {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Ciphermaniac's Codebreaking|145}} increases the damage dealt by {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Valiant|80}} or can set up a strong attack from {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Thorns|62}}, the latter of which discards Future cards from the top of the player's deck. The {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Future Booster Energy Capsule|164}}, which has also been reprinted in Temporal Forces, can further increase the damage dealt by Future Pokémon and allows {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Treads|118}} to gain the {{TCG|Fighting}} type.

Temporal Forces includes cards from the Japanese Wild Force and Cyber Judge expansions as well as the Japanese {{TCG|Starter Deck & Build Sets}}. This set includes seven {{TCG|ACE SPEC card|ACE SPEC}} Trainer and Special Energy cards, thirteen {{TCG|Pokémon ex}}, two Tera Pokémon ex, 22 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, 18 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, ten {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and six {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards. The illustration rare prints of {{TCG ID|Wild Force|Flutter Mane|76}} from Wild Force and {{TCG ID|Cyber Judge|Iron Thorns|77}} from Cyber Judge are not present in Temporal Forces; they are instead {{TCG|SVP Black Star Promos}} and appear in the {{p|Walking Wake}} and {{p|Iron Leaves}} {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|Temporal Forces Elite Trainer Box}}es respectively.

Temporal Forces is available in English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, and Portuguese.

