'''Transformation Mask''' (Japanese: '''変幻の仮面''') is the name given to the sixth Japanese expansion of cards released during the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s {{TCG|Scarlet & Violet Era}}.

==Information==
Like the previously released set, {{TCG|Crimson Haze}}, '''Transformation Mask''' focuses on various Pokémon, characters, and settings from the land of [[Kitakami]], which debuted in [[The Teal Mask]], the first part of [[The Hidden Treasure of Area Zero]] DLC for the [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]] video games. The primary focus of the set is {{p|Ogerpon}}, which appears in all of its special {{Tera}}stallized forms. Additionally, the [[Loyal Three]] debut in this set, while [[Carmine]] and [[Kieran]] appear as {{TCG|Supporter card}}s. The set also continues to introduce {{TCG|ACE SPEC card}}s into the format, including one ACE SPEC {{TCG|Special Energy card}}.

Each form of Ogerpon appears as a {{DL|Pokémon ex (TCG)|Tera Pokémon ex}}, and players can swap between their various Ogerpon ex using the {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Ogre's Mask|159}} card. Using {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Teal Mask Ogerpon|24}}, players can add {{TCG|Basic Grass Energy}} to their hand, which can be attached using {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Teal Mask Ogerpon ex|25}}'s {{TCG|Ability}} to strengthen its own attack as well as {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Sinistcha|22}}'s attack. Additionally, the Pokémon {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Dipplin|18}}, {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Goldeen|44}}, and {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Swirlix|89}} have the {{cw|Festival Lead}} Ability, which allows them to attack consecutively while {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Festival Grounds|149}} is in play; this also enables {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Thwackey|15}} to search the deck while one of them is in the Active Spot. Furthermore, {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Munkidori|95}}, {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Fezandipiti|96}}, and {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Okidogi|111}} each have Abilities that trigger while {{TCG|Darkness}} Energy is attached to them, although none of these cards are Darkness-type.

Transformation Mask contains three {{TCG|ACE SPEC card|ACE SPEC}} Trainer and Special Energy cards, three Pokémon ex, five Tera Pokémon ex, 12 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, 11 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, six {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Transformation Mask was released in Japanese on April 26, 2024, followed by localized releases in Traditional Chinese on May 10, 2024, in Thai on May 31, 2024, and in Korean on June 21, 2024. The Indonesian set equivalent, {{ATCG|Transfiguration Mask}}, released on the same day as the Thai release. The Traditional Chinese release is accompanied with the release of the '''Transformation Mask Collector's Set''' (Traditional Chinese: '''變幻假面 收藏家組合''' ''Transformation Mask Collector's Set''), a product which contains 10 booster packs, a card list booklet, and a stamped Full Art promo card of {{TCG ID|SV-P Promo|Chansey|99}}.

Cards released in this set are included in the English {{TCG|Twilight Masquerade}} expansion. The illustration rare prints of {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Munkidori|107}}, {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Fezandipiti|108}}, and {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Okidogi|110}} from this set are excluded from Twilight Masquerade and instead appear in {{TCG|Shrouded Fable}}.

