'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Twilight Masquerade''''' is the sixth main expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released on May 24, 2024.

==Blurb==
<i>A Festival of Mischief & Mystery!

Welcome to the land of Kitakami, where people and Pokémon live harmoniously with nature. Folktales abound, but not all is as it seems... Uncover the mystery of the masked Legendary Pokémon Ogerpon, appearing as four fearsome types of Tera Pokémon ex, and team up with more newly discovered Pokémon, like Bloodmoon Ursaluna ex and Sinistcha ex. Growing in power, Greninja, Dragapult, and Magcargo dazzle as Tera Pokémon ex, and more ACE SPEC cards round out the festivities in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Twilight Masquerade expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Twilight Masquerade''' focuses on various Pokémon, characters, and settings from the land of [[Kitakami]], which debuted in [[The Teal Mask]], the first part of [[The Hidden Treasure of Area Zero]] DLC for the [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]] video games. The primary focus of the set is {{p|Ogerpon}}, which appears in all of its special {{Tera}}stallized forms. Other Kitakami Pokémon debuting include the [[Loyal Three]], {{form|Ursaluna|Bloodmoon}} {{p|Ursaluna}}, {{p|Dipplin}}, and {{p|Sinistcha}}. [[Carmine]], [[Kieran]], and [[Perrin]] appear as {{TCG|Supporter card}}s. The set also continues to introduce {{TCG|ACE SPEC card}}s into the format, including one ACE SPEC {{TCG|Special Energy card}}.

Each form of Ogerpon appears as a {{DL|Pokémon ex (TCG)|Tera Pokémon ex}}, and players can swap between their various Ogerpon ex using the {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Ogre's Mask|159}} card. Using {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Teal Mask Ogerpon|24}}, players can add {{TCG|Basic Grass Energy}} to their hand, which can be attached using {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Teal Mask Ogerpon ex|25}}'s {{TCG|Ability}} to strengthen its own attack as well as {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Sinistcha|22}}'s attack. Additionally, the Pokémon {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Dipplin|18}}, {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Goldeen|44}}, and {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Swirlix|89}} have the {{cw|Festival Lead}} Ability, which allows them to attack consecutively while {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Festival Grounds|149}} is in play; this also enables {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Thwackey|15}} to search the deck while one of them is in the Active Spot. Furthermore, {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Munkidori|95}}, {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Fezandipiti|96}}, and {{TCG ID|Twilight Masquerade|Okidogi|111}} each have Abilities that trigger while {{TCG|Darkness}} Energy is attached to them, although none of these cards are Darkness-type.

Twilight Masquerade includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Transformation Mask}} and {{TCG|Crimson Haze}} expansions. This set contains six {{TCG|ACE SPEC card|ACE SPEC}} Trainer and Special Energy cards, seven Pokémon ex, seven Tera Pokémon ex, 21 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, 12 {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, 11 {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and six {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards. The illustration rare prints of {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Munkidori|107}}, {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Fezandipiti|108}}, and {{TCG ID|Transformation Mask|Okidogi|110}} from Transformation Mask are excluded from this set and instead appear in {{TCG|Shrouded Fable}}.

Twilight Masquerade is available in English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, and Portuguese.

