'''Wild Force''' (Japanese: '''ワイルドフォース''') and '''Cyber Judge''' (Japanese: '''サイバージャッジ''') are the names given to the two Japanese paired sets that collectively make up the fifth Japanese expansion of cards released during the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s {{TCG|Scarlet & Violet Era}}.

==Information==
The '''Wild Force''' and '''Cyber Judge''' sets continue to introduce {{TCG|Ancient}} and {{TCG|Future}} Pokémon and Trainer cards into the Pokémon Trading Card Game. Each set focuses on a trio of [[Paradox Pokémon]]. Wild Force features the Ancient Pokémon resembling the [[Legendary beasts]], {{p|Walking Wake}}, {{p|Gouging Fire}}, and {{p|Raging Bolt}}, while Cyber Judge features the Future Pokémon resembling the [[Swords of Justice]], {{p|Iron Leaves}}, {{p|Iron Boulder}}, and {{p|Iron Crown}}.

These sets also reintroduced {{TCG|ACE SPEC card}}s. First introduced in the Black & White Series of the TCG, ACE SPEC cards are powerful cards with the restriction that only one ACE SPEC card of any sort can be included in a deck. ACE SPEC cards as of this set have a unique magenta design and may be {{TCG|Trainer card}}s or {{TCG|Special Energy card}}s.

Playing multiple Ancient Pokémon from Wild Force together increases the damage {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Koraidon|119}} can deal and allows more cards to be drawn with the ACE SPEC {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Awakening Drum|141}}. Using the {{TCG|Supporter card}} {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Explorer's Guidance|147}} allows {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Great Tusk|97}} to discard more cards from the opponent's deck, while {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Roaring Moon|109}} can deal more damage with more Ancient cards in the player's discard pile. These Pokémon can also increase their defensive capability using the {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Ancient Booster Energy Capsule|159}}, which has been reprinted in this set. The Future Pokémon from Cyber Judge can deal more damage while {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Crown ex|81}} is in play, and additional Energy can be attached to them using {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Miraidon|121}} and the ACE SPEC {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Reboot Pod|158}}. Playing the Supporter card {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Ciphermaniac's Codebreaking|145}} increases the damage dealt by {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Valiant|80}} or can set up a strong attack from {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Thorns|62}}, the latter of which discards Future cards from the top of the player's deck. The {{TCG ID|Paradox Rift|Future Booster Energy Capsule|164}}, which has been reprinted in this set, can further increase the damage dealt by Future Pokémon and allows {{TCG ID|Temporal Forces|Iron Treads|118}} to gain the {{TCG|Fighting}} type.

Each set contains three {{TCG|ACE SPEC card}}s, five {{TCG|Pokémon ex}}, one Tera Pokémon ex, 12 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, nine {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards, five {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Wild Force and Cyber Judge were released in Japanese on January 26, 2024, followed by localized releases in {{pmin|Chinese|Traditional Chinese}} on February 2, 2024, in {{pmin|Thailand|Thai}} on February 23, 2024, and in {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} on March 6, 2024. The {{pmin|Indonesia}}n set equivalent, {{ATCG|Ace Paradox}}, released on March 29, 2024.

Cards released in this set are included in the English {{TCG|Temporal Forces}} expansion. The illustration rare prints of {{TCG ID|Wild Force|Flutter Mane|76}} from Wild Force and {{TCG ID|Cyber Judge|Iron Thorns|77}} from Cyber Judge are not present in Temporal Forces; they are instead {{TCG|SVP Black Star Promos}} and appear in the {{p|Walking Wake}} and {{p|Iron Leaves}} {{TCGMerch|Scarlet & Violet|Series|Temporal Forces Elite Trainer Box}}es respectively.

