'''Burning Confrontation''' (Korean: '''불꽃 튀는 대결''' ''Bulkkot Twineun Daegyeol'') is the name given to the second extension set of cards from the DP Series of the {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The set continues to feature {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} for the Korean Card Game and introduce [[Generation IV]] overall. Still not providing Pokémon of the {{ct|Psychic}}, {{ct|Fighting}}, {{ct|Darkness}}, or {{ct|Metal}}, this set of cards focuses on strengthening the five types included within {{KTCG|Start of an Adventure}} and its four accompanying Random Decks.

==Information==
'''Burning Confrontation''' is the second Korean extension set of cards after the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] went into hiatus until the middle of 2010. Released June 17, 2010, this extension set continues to introduce both new [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and new {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the Korean Card Game. In order to provide players with more meaningful options for their limited card pool at the time of release, it focuses exclusively on the {{ct|Grass}}, {{ct|Fire}}, {{ct|Water}}, {{ct|Lightning}}, and {{ct|Colorless}}, saving the other four types for the third extension set: {{KTCG|Space-Time Clash}}.

Included in the Burning Confrontation set are 40 cards originating from the early half of the English Diamond & Pearl Series. The set pulls its Ultra-Rare {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} focus from the {{TCG|Mysterious Treasures}} expansion, but contains a majority of cards from the {{TCG|Diamond & Pearl}} and {{TCG|Secret Wonders}} expansions. Only {{TCG ID|Mysterious Treasures|Magmortar LV.X|123}} and {{TCG ID|Mysterious Treasures|Electivire LV.X|121}} are included, with {{TCG ID|Mysterious Treasures|Lucario LV.X|122}} being utilized later as it falls outside of the extension's type focus.

The only [[Legendary Pokémon]] included in the set are the {{ct|Colorless}} {{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Latias|22}}
and {{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Latios|23}} from {{TCG|Great Encounters}}, which, as {{t|Dragon}}-types, utilize only the four types of Energy released thus far in the DP Series. {{TCG|Supporter card}}s and one {{TCG|Stadium card}} premier in this extension, after not being included in {{KTCG|Start of an Adventure}}. Despite being released during [[Generation IV]], {{p|Magmortar}}, {{p|Electivire}} and {{p|Munchlax}} are the only [[Sinnoh]] natives to be included in the expansion, though the two former as the set's Ultra-Rare cards. These two Pokémon as well as the two Legendary Pokémon are elevated to [[Holographic card|Holofoil]] status, a trait that {{p|Latias}}, {{p|Latios}}, and {{p|Magmortar}} lacked in English (Magmortar dropping its Holofoil quality from the Japanese {{TCG|Magmortar vs Electivire Deck Kit}} release).

