'''Pokémon TCG: ''Mega Evolution—Chaos Rising''''' is the fourth main expansion of cards from the Mega Evolution Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The expansion continues the [[Pokémon Legends: Z-A]] theming and introduces more Mega Evolution Pokémon ex, among them Mega {{p|Greninja}} ex and Mega {{p|Floette}} ex. It was released on May 22, 2026.

==Blurb==
<i><b>Take On the Challenge of an Eternity!</b>

The hustle and bustle of the city turns into havoc as Mega Floette ex brings turmoil to the streets! Filled with courage and determination, Mega Greninja ex gathers other powerful Mega Evolution Pokémon ex, including Mega Pyroar ex and Mega Dragalge ex, to ward off this growing threat. As night falls, danger blossoms in the Pokémon TCG: Mega Evolution—Chaos Rising expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Chaos Rising''' is the fourth main expansion of cards for the Mega Evolution Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. It is the second main set to be based on the video game {{g|Legends: Z-A}}, and the third overall after {{TCG|Ascended Heroes}} and {{TCG|Perfect Order}}. The central Pokémon featured in this set include {{TCG ID|Chaos Rising|Mega Greninja ex|22}} and {{TCG ID|Chaos Rising|Mega Floette ex|35}}.<ref name="TPCi 20260312"/>

Chaos Rising includes cards released in the Japanese {{TCG|Ninja Spinner}} expansion. Chaos Rising features more than 120 cards,<ref name=Pokemon.com20260312/> including five Mega Evolution Pokémon ex, five Pokémon ex, 11 illustration rare Pokémon, 18 ultra rare Pokémon and Trainer cards, and six special illustration rare Pokémon and Supporter cards.<ref name="TPCi 20260312"/> All Rares and below of this expansion are also available as Reverse Holofoil versions.

Chaos Rising released worldwide on May 22, 2026.<ref name="TPCi 20260312"/>

