'''Collection 151''' (Simplified Chinese: '''收集啦151''') is the first subset of cards to be released in the {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} Scarlet & Violet era of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]].

==Information==
'''Collection 151''' is a special expansion featuring all 151 Pokémon from [[Generation I]] in [[National Pokédex]] order, rather than being sorted by type first, as Pokémon cards usually would. It was revealed on December 22, 2024, as part of the introduction of the Scarlet & Violet era in the Simplified Chinese language, and was first released on January 17, 2025.

Although the set is the equivalent of the Japanese {{TCG|Pokémon Card 151}} and international {{TCG|151}} expansions, a number of changes were made to its card list:
* all {{TCG|Trainer}} cards were removed, leaving only Pokémon cards;
* all 18 {{TCG|illustration rare card}}s (with an '''AR''' rarity) from the original expansion were removed;
* 18 {{TCG|shiny rare}} cards (with an '''S''' rarity), all of which are reprints from this expansion originating from {{TCG|Shiny Treasure ex}}, were added;
* the {{TCG|special illustration rare}} prints of {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Venusaur ex|3}}, {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Charizard ex|6}}, and {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Blastoise ex|9}} were removed;
* the {{TCG|shiny ultra rare}} prints of {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Wigglytuff ex|186}}, {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Alakazam ex|187}}, and {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Mew ex|188}} from Shiny Treasure ex were added;
* the {{TCG|special illustration rare}} print of {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Mew ex|191}} from Shiny Treasure ex was added;
* four {{TCG|illustration rare}} prints of {{TCG ID|Collection 151|Pikachu|25}}, each illustrated by [[Oswaldo KATO]], were added and are currently exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language.

Each of the 139 Common, Uncommon, and Rare cards in the expansion also comes in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and a rarer one with a Master Ball motif:

