'''Colorful Legends''' (Korean: '''화려한 전설''' ''Hwaryeohan Jeonseol'') is the name given to the eighth extension set of cards from the DP Series of the {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The set continues to feature {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}}. This set does not focus on a specific type.

==Information==
'''Colorful Legends''' is the eighth Korean extension set of cards after the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] went into hiatus until the middle of 2010. Released December 16, 2010, this extension set continues to introduce both new [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and new {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the Korean Card Game. This set does not focus on any particular type, even though there is slightly more {{ct|Grass}} cards.

Included in the Colorful Legends set are 40 cards originating from the early half of the English Diamond & Pearl Series. The set pulls its Ultra-Rare {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} focus from the {{TCG|Platinum}} and {{TCG|Stormfront}} expansions and contains a majority of cards from the {{TCG|Mysterious Treasures}} and {{TCG|Secret Wonders}} expansions.

The only [[Legendary Pokémon]] included in the set are {{p|Shaymin}}, {{p|Entei}}, {{p|Suicune}}, {{p|Raikou}}, and {{p|Mew}}.

