Crosstrainer (TCG):
'''Crosstrainer''' is the name given to an unreleased {{TCG|Base Set}} revision produced by [[Wizards of the Coast]]. Crosstrainer was to include each of the first 150 [[Generation I]] {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}, from {{p|Bulbasaur}} to {{p|Mewtwo}}, as well a number of {{TCG|Trainer}} and {{TCG|Energy card}}s.<ref name=chatlog>[https://compendium.pokegym.net/chatlogs/Chat_2001_03_15.htm Pokemon Chat Report - Thursday, March 15, 2001]{{sic}}</ref> It has been estimated that the set would have included around 170 cards.

Originally reported for a North American release in April 2001,<ref name=aaah>[https://www.pokemonaaah.com/pokemon/index3.html Pokémon Aaah! | New "Tournament" Set - Monday, March 5, 2001]</ref> Crosstrainer was eventually delayed to July 10, 2001;{{fact}} however, it was never released. It would have been the 10th English expansion, following {{TCG|Neo Discovery}}. Because Crosstrainer was developed by Wizards, it was never planned to be released in Japan. Crosstrainer went through a number of name changes since it was first announced, including ''Pokémon X'', ''Tournament Set'',<ref name=aaah/> and ''Base Set 3''.<ref name=aaah/>

Crosstrainer was intended to be a new Base Set revision, building upon the standards set by {{TCG|Base Set 2}}. It was said to include cards from Base Set 2 (itself composed of {{TCG|Base Set}} and {{TCG|Jungle}}), {{TCG|Fossil}}, and {{TCG|Team Rocket}}, as well as approximately 30 {{TCG|Vending Machine cards}}.<ref name=chatlog/> Other rumors had said that Crosstrainer was going to include cards from {{TCG|Gym Heroes}} and {{TCG|Gym Challenge}}, but it was very unlikely. The makeup of the set was designed for play in a {{TCG|sealed format}}, as well as compatibility with the Neo Series.<ref name=chatlog/>

Crosstrainer was ultimately axed from Wizards' product line up in the summer of 2001. Wizards representatives said that the company wanted to instead focus on releasing the {{TCG|Southern Islands}} promotional set and {{TCG|Neo Revelation}}. It is rumored that Nintendo did not want Wizards of the Coast to release a new Base Set revision at the time.

Although Crosstrainer was never released, the concept of another Base Set revision lived on in {{TCG|Legendary Collection}}. Wizards of the Coast attempted to release Vending Machine cards again in {{TCG|Jamboree}}, another unreleased set. An expansion consisting of each first generation of Pokémon was eventually released as {{TCG|151}}, over twenty years later.

