'''Dark Crescent''' (Korean: '''암흑의 초승달''' ''Amheug-ui Choseungdal'') is the name given to the sixth extension set of cards from the DP Series of the {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The set continues to feature {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} for the Korean Card Game. This set does not focus on any one type in particular.

==Information==
'''Dark Crescent''' is the sixth Korean extension set of cards after the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] went into hiatus until the middle of 2010. Released November 11, 2010, this extension set continues to introduce both new [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and new {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the Korean Card Game. This set has a wide variety of types featured, but it contains slightly more {{ct|Psychic}} cards.

Included in the Dark Crescent set are 60 cards originating from the early half of the English Diamond & Pearl Series. The set pulls its {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} from the {{TCG|Great Encounters}} and {{TCG|Legends Awakened}} expansions, but contains a majority of cards from the {{TCG|Mysterious Treasures}} and {{TCG|Secret Wonders}} expansions.

The only [[Legendary Pokémon]] included in the set are {{p|Cresselia}} and {{p|Darkrai}}, which are included twice ({{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Cresselia|2}} and {{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Cresselia LV.X|103}}, {{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Darkrai|4}} and {{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Darkrai LV.X|104}}). {{TCG|Cyclone Energy}} and {{TCG|Warp Energy}} premier in this extension.

