'''Pokémon TCG: ''Mega Evolution—Delta Reign''''' is the sixth main expansion of cards from the Mega Evolution Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The expansion is based on {{me|Rayquaza}} ex. It will be released on November 6, 2026.

==Blurb==
<i><b>A Legendary Storm Is Stirring!</b>

A thunderous roar from above heralds the descent of a renowned ruler of the sky! Mega Rayquaza ex brings unparalleled strength to battle, inspiring Mega Golurk ex, Mega Malamar ex, and Mega Golisopod ex to come forth and put their own skills to the test. Prevailing winds lead to legendary places and emerald-colored storms in the Pokémon TCG: Mega Evolution—Delta Reign expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Delta Reign''' is the sixth main expansion of cards for the Mega Evolution Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game, featuring {{TCG ID|Delta Reign|Mega Rayquaza ex|84}} as the central Pokémon. In addition to introducing more {{TCG|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} to the game, Delta Reign also introduces "Legendary Stadiums", which are Stadium cards that are played together as a pair. Legendary Stadiums have {{TCG|combined illustration}}s between the pair of cards that form them. Any Delta Reign booster pack containing a Legendary Stadium will contain both halves of each pair.<ref name="TPCi 20260820"/>

Delta Reign includes cards released in the Japanese {{TCG|Storm Emeralda}} expansion and the 2026 Japanese {{TCG|ex Starter Sets 2026|ex Starter Sets}}. Delta Reign features more than 135 cards,<ref name=Pokemon.com20260820/> including four Mega Evolution Pokémon ex, six Pokémon ex, six Stadium cards creating three Legendary Stadiums, 14 illustration rare Pokémon, 17 ultra rare Pokémon and Trainer cards, and six special illustration rare Pokémon and Supporter cards.<ref name="TPCi 20260820"/> Delta Reign will be released worldwide on November 6, 2026.<ref name="TPCi 20260820"/>

Delta Reign was first revealed on June 18, 2026, at the same time as Storm Emeralda and {{TCGP|Ruler of the Skies}}, the latter being a Rayquaza-themed set for [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]].

