'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Destined Rivals''''' is the name of the tenth and final main expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released in English on May 30, 2025.

==Blurb==
<i>Whose Side Are You On?

Pokémon Trainers, be on high alert! The nefarious Team Rocket is setting its latest plan into motion, and heroic Trainers are racing to stop it. Join forces with the likes of Cynthia and Garchomp ex, Ethan and Ho-Oh ex, or Arven and Mabosstiff ex… Or reconsider your loyalties and fight alongside Team Rocket’s Pokémon like Mewtwo ex—under the command of Giovanni! Choose a side, assemble your allies, and battle boldly in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Destined Rivals expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Destined Rivals''' is the tenth main expansion of cards for the Scarlet & Violet Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. It continues the release of {{TCG|Trainer's Pokémon}}, with an emphasis on [[Team Rocket]]. Other featured Trainers include [[Cynthia]], [[Ethan]], [[Arven]], [[Misty]], [[Marnie]], and [[Steven Stone]].

Destined Rivals includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Hot Wind Arena}} subset, the {{TCG|Glory of the Rocket Gang}} expansion, and the two ex Starter Sets for {{TCG|ex Starter Set Marnie's Morpeko & Grimmsnarl ex|Marnie's Morpeko & Grimmsnarl ex}} and {{TCG|ex Starter Set Steven's Beldum & Metagross ex|Steven's Beldum & Metagross ex}}. The expansion includes 182 regular cards, with more than 240 cards total after {{TCG|secret card}}s are included. Cards from the expansion were made available before the release date starting May 16, 2025 in the {{TCG|Marnie Rival Battle Deck|Marnie}} and {{TCG|Steven Rival Battle Deck}}s.

The expansion includes 83 cards relating to Team Rocket, including more than 45 Team Rocket's Pokémon; more than 85 Trainer's Pokémon, including the aforementioned Team Rocket's Pokémon; 17 Pokémon ex, including 10 Trainer's Pokémon ex; more than 20 Trainer cards; more than 45 cards with special illustrations, including 23 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon cards and 11 {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon cards; and six {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

The {{TCG|booster pack}} artworks feature [[Giovanni]] and {{p|Mewtwo}}, [[Cynthia]] and her {{TP|Cynthia|Garchomp}}, {{ga|Ethan}} and his {{p|Ho-Oh}}, and various [[Team Rocket]] members and their Pokémon. The four artworks, and an additional Team Rocket-themed artwork, were featured on the passes given for buying tickets to [https://latam.gamescom.global/en/home/ gamescom latam 2025]. The organization posted images on February 19, 2025 ahead of the official reveal<ref>[https://x.com/PokeGuardian/status/1891884660470255763 PokeGuardian Twitter]</ref>, only for them to be removed the next day.

