'''Sun & Moon: Double Burst''' is the name given to the fifth of six Asian Sun & Moon Era catch-up sets in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It is exclusively available in Traditional Chinese and {{pmin|Thailand|Thai}}. The Indonesian counterpart collection to this set is the {{ATCG|Tag Team Collection}}. It is the third expansion to be released in Traditional Chinese.

==Information==
[[File:Double Burst Logo Thai.png|thumb|left|170px|Thai logo]]
'''Double Burst''' was first released on February 18, 2020 in Taiwan and Hong Kong, utilizing the AS set prefix instead of the previous AC prefix. It was subsequently released in Thailand on February 27, 2020. This set is composed of cards sourced from the Japanese {{TCG|Tag Bolt}} and {{TCG|Double Blaze}} expansions, as well as the associated {{TCG|Night Unison}}, {{TCG|Full Metal Wall}}, and {{TCG|GG End}} subsets, focusing heavily on {{TCG|TAG TEAM}} {{TCG|Pokémon-GX}}. It is split into two sets, Set A and Set B, each of which focuses on specific types. Set A features {{ct|Grass}}, {{ct|Water}}, {{ct|Lightning}}, {{ct|Darkness}}, and {{ct|Dragon}} Pokémon, while Set B features {{ct|Fire}}, {{ct|Psychic}}, {{ct|Fighting}}, {{ct|Metal}}, {{ct|Fairy}}, and {{ct|Dragon}} Pokémon. The booster pack art for each set features specially commissioned illustrations by [[Mitsuhiro Arita]] and are based on the those from the Japanese Tag Bolt and Double Blaze expansions. Each pack contains six cards.

