'''Pokémon TCG: ''Double Crisis''''' (Japanese: '''コンセプトパック マグマ団VSアクア団 ダブルクライシス''' ''Concept Pack Magma Gang VS Aqua Gang: Double Crisis'') is a special expansion of cards from the XY Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released as the first subset from the XY Era of the Pokémon Card Game in Japan.

==Blurb==
<i>Rival Ambitions: Aqua vs. Magma!

Two teams of villains emerge from their hideouts to clash over the fate of the world in Pokémon TCG: Double Crisis! Team Aqua brings sheer brawn and willpower while Team Magma leverages logic, and both are willing to move land and sea to accomplish their goals. While Team Aqua's Kyogre-EX rampages against Team Magma's Groudon-EX, their rival ambitions could change the Hoenn region forever!</i>

==Information==
[[File:CP1 Logo.png|200px|thumb|Magma Gang VS Aqua Gang:<br>Double Crisis logo]]
'''Double Crisis''' is a special expansion of the ''XY Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Magma Gang VS Aqua Gang: Double Crisis''', the first subset in the Pokémon Card Game XY Era.

Double Crisis featured the two [[Villainous team|villainous organizations]] of the [[Hoenn]] [[region]], [[Team Aqua]] and [[Team Magma]].

The card design was visually enhanced. Pokémon displayed their respective Team's logo on the attack box and a headshot of a Grunt on the right of the Pokédex entry. Trainer cards also sported their respective Team's logo in the description box.

Unlike regular expansions, Double Crisis booster packs could not be purchased individually from booster boxes. Instead, they were only made available in the {{TCGMerch|XY|Series|Double Crisis Blisters}} released on March 25, 2015. Each booster pack contained seven cards.

The Japanese subset was released on January 30, 2015.

