'''Pokémon TCG: ''Dragon Vault''''' (Japanese: '''拡張パック ドラゴンセレクション''' ''Expansion Pack Dragon Selection'') is a special expansion of cards of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan it was released as the first subset from the BW Era.

==Blurb==
<i>Open the Vault and Let Loose the Dragons... for the Very First Time!

The vault echoes with the roar of Dragons—can you train what you find within? Inside the Pokémon TCG: Dragon Vault, you'll discover a treasure trove you've never seen before! You'll find incredible Dragon Pokémon such as Rayquaza and Druddigon—ALL of them foil!—in special 5-card booster packs, plus a code card to unlock hoards of rewards for the Pokémon TCG Online. So, when you open the vault, be prepared to command the might of these powerful Dragon Pokémon!</i>

==Information==
[[File:Dragon Selection Logo.png|200px|thumb|Dragon Selection logo]]
'''Dragon Vault''' released a special expansion of the of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Dragon Selection''', the first subset in the Pokémon Card Game BW Era. Dragon Vault introduced {{TCG|Dragon}} Pokémon.

The expansion was originally released as part of the "''Dragon Vault Series''"<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20121028140947/http://www.pokemon.com/us/pokemon-trading-card-game/pokemon-trading-card-expansions/ Pokémon Trading Card Expansions (Archive from October 28, 2012)]</ref> where it was the only entry. By May 2013, the official website had begun listing the expansion alongside the Black and White Series, which it continues to do to this day. <ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20130527043411/http://www.pokemon.com/us/pokemon-trading-card-game/pokemon-trading-card-expansions/ Pokémon Trading Card Expansions (Archive from May 27, 2013)]</ref>

Unlike regular expansions, Dragon Vault booster packs could not be purchased individually from booster boxes. Instead, they were only made available in the {{TCGMerch|Black & White|Series|Dragon Vault Blisters}} released on October 5, 2012. Each booster pack contained 5 Holofoil cards. The Japanese subset was released on January 27, 2012.

The year on which Dragon Vault was released, 2012, is also the {{wp|Dragon (zodiac)|Year of the Dragon}} according to the {{wp|Chinese calendar}}.

