'''Pokémon TCG: ''EX Crystal Guardians''''' (Japanese: '''きせきの結晶''' ''Miracle Crystal'') is the name given to the fourteenth main expansion of cards from the EX Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It is the eighth main expansion from the PCG Era of the Pokémon Card Game in Japan. The set continues to feature [[Generation III]] Pokémon, {{TCG|Pokémon-ex}}, and {{TCG|Pokémon ☆}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>ONLY THE BEST SHALL PASS THE CRYSTAL GUARDIANS

A remote island... mysterious crystals... and incredible Pokémon just waiting for you to discover them! EX Crystal Guardians takes you to distant shores where more new Pokémon Delta Species, Pokémon-ex, and Pokémon{{Star}} live among astonishing crystals that can change how Trainers do battle. Are you ready to explore the island and capture your favorite Crystal Guardians?</i>

==Information==
'''EX Crystal Guardians''' is the name given to the fourteenth main expansion of the ''EX Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Miracle Crystal''', the eighth expansion in the Pokémon Card Game PCG Era. This set features [[Generation III]] Pokémon. The English expansion was released on August 30, 2006, while the Japanese expansion was released on March 10, 2006.

Prerelease events were held during the weekends of August 12th-13th, August 19th-20th and August 26th-27th.<ref>https://web.archive.org/web/20070425142016/http://op.pokemon-tcg.com/events/locator/?event_type=36&location=north_america</ref>

The expansion was set on a mysterious island, far from the city of [[Holon]], where Pokémon, both regular and Delta Species, live in harmony. The island also bears naturally growing crystals, which were said to grant special powers if used correctly.

This is the last expansion to feature dual-type Pokémon {{TCG|δ Delta Species}}.

