'''Pokémon-e TCG: ''EX Team Magma vs Team Aqua''''' (Japanese: '''強化拡張パックex1 マグマVSアクア ふたつの野望''' ''Enhanced Expansion Pack ex1 Magma VS Aqua: Two Ambitions'') is the name given to the fourth main expansion of cards from the EX Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released as the only subset from the ADV Era of the Pokémon Card Game in Japan. The set continues to feature [[Generation III]] Pokémon and {{TCG|Pokémon-ex}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>Lead your Team to victory!

Get ready for exciting, new head-to-head battles with the EX Team Magma vs Team Aqua expansion. Pick a side, then equip yourself with a powerful mix of new Pokémon-ex Evolution cards and all-new Dual Energy type Pokémon. Every team needs a hero. You're it!</i>

==Information==
'''EX Team Magma vs Team Aqua''' is the name given to the fourth main expansion of the ''EX Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Magma VS Aqua: Two Ambitions''', the only subset in the Pokémon Card Game ADV Era. It is based on {{game|Ruby and Sapphire|s}}, featuring [[Generation III]] Pokémon and the two [[villainous team]]s of the [[Hoenn]] region [[Team Magma]] and [[Team Aqua]]. The English expansion was released on March 15, 2004, while the Japanese subset was released on October 24, 2003.

EX Team Magma vs Team Aqua introduced {{cat|dual-type Pokémon cards}}, which have two types. The {{TCG|Owner's Pokémon}} mechanic returned in the EX Series with {{DL|Owner's Pokémon|Team Magma's Pokémon}} and {{DL|Owner's Pokémon|Team Aqua's Pokémon}}.

The card design is visually enhanced for Pokémon belonging to their respective teams. Team Magma's Pokémon have curvy lines on the border of the artwork window, while Team Aqua's Pokémon have bubbles on it. The Pokémon type symbol on the top right corner of the card has a different base for each team. Pokémon belonging to a team display that team's logo on the bottom right of the attack box. All of Team Magma's Pokémon and Team Aqua's Pokémon have CG illustrations.

Cards associated with Team Aqua or Team Magma do not feature [[e-Reader]] dot code strips. This is the final expansion to include dot code strips on any cards.

A {{TCG|Box Topper}}, {{TCG ID|EX Team Magma vs Team Aqua|Absol|96}}, was also featured for the first time since the {{TCG|Skyridge}} expansion. This was the first Box Topper to be a normally-sized {{TCG|secret card}}.

