'''Pokémon TCG: ''EX Team Rocket Returns''''' (Japanese: '''ロケット団の逆襲''' ''Rocket Gang Strikes Back'') is the name given to the seventh main expansion of cards from the EX Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It is the third main expansion from the PCG Era of the Pokémon Card Game in Japan. The set continues to feature {{TCG|Pokémon-ex}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>BACK WITH A VENGEANCE!

The return of Team Rocket is trouble for your opponents. Jessie and James are back and up to old tricks, with some of the most ruthless Pokémon ever at their side. If you can master Team Rocket's way, their all-new Dark Pokémon and Pokémon-ex can carry you to victory!</i>

==Information==
'''EX Team Rocket Returns''' is the name given to the seventh main expansion of the ''EX Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Rocket Gang Strikes Back''', the third expansion in the Pokémon Card Game PCG Era. It is seemingly based on the return of [[Team Rocket]], as depicted in [[Pokémon Gold|Gold]], [[Pokémon Silver|Silver]], and [[Pokémon Crystal|Crystal]]. It features both [[Generation I]] and [[Generation II]] Pokémon. The English expansion was released on November 8, 2004, while the Japanese expansion was released on October 15, 2004.

EX Team Rocket Returns introduced {{TCG|Pokémon ☆}}, a type of Pokémon with {{Shiny|different coloration}} to what is usual for its species. Pokémon ☆ had part of the Pokémon out of the artwork window border and the rarity symbol was gold foil.

Rocket's Pokémon-ex had spikes on the border of the artwork window and for the base of the Pokémon type symbol. The Team Rocket logo was displayed on the bottom right of the attack box. Reverse Holofoil from this expansion onward featured the set logo on the bottom right corner of the artwork. Reverse Holofoil versions of the Rare and Rare Holo cards have gold foil name text and rarity symbol.

