'''Scarlet & Violet: Fearless Terastal''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 无畏太晶''') is the third {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet Series.

== Information ==
[[File:CSV3 banner.png|thumb|300px|Set banner artwork]]
'''Fearless Terastal''' is the third Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. The expansion introduces {{DL|Pokémon ex (TCG)|Tera Pokémon ex}} to the game, depicting Pokémon which have undergone [[Terastallization]] as seen in [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]]; these Pokémon ex have a permanent effect which prevents them from taking direct damage while on the player's [[Bench]].

Most of the set's cards originate from the Japanese {{TCG|Scarlet & Violet}}, {{TCG|Snow Hazard}}, {{TCG|Clay Burst}} and {{TCG|Ruler of the Black Flame}} expansions, with a small number of cards from the {{TCG|ex Start Decks}}, {{TCG|Ancient Roar}}, and {{TCG|Future Flash}} also included, though no {{TCG|Ancient}} or {{TCG|Future}} cards from the latter two sets are present. The expansion focuses on the Tera Pokémon ex {{OBP|Arcanine ex|Fearless Terastal 18}} as well as the [[treasures of ruin]], the latter of which were also the focus of the Japanese {{TCG|Snow Hazard}}, {{TCG|Clay Burst}}, and English {{TCG|Paldea Evolved}} expansions.

Fearless Terastal features one card exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language: a {{TCG|special illustration rare}} print of {{TCG ID|Fearless Terastal|Arcanine ex|155}}.

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 130 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and one with a rarer Master Ball motif.
