'''Pokémon TCG: ''XY—Flashfire''''' (Japanese: '''ワイルドブレイズ''' ''Wild Blaze'') is the name given to the second main expansion of cards from the XY Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] (the XY Era in Japan). The set continues to feature [[Generation VI]] Pokémon, {{TCG|Pokémon-EX|Pokémon-EX, and M Pokémon-EX}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>Reign with Fire!

Blaze your way to glory and watch the sparks fly when you play Pokémon TCG: XY—Flashfire! Ignite the action with a firestorm of Fire types and watch your opponents' terrified double-take as the awesome Mega Charizard-EX makes its scorching debut in this breathtaking expansion! Your explosive adventures will continue as your foes flee the field with certain doom flashing before their eyes!</i>
{{-}}

==Information==
[[File:XY2 Logo.png|200px|thumb|Wild Blaze logo]]
'''Flashfire''' is the name given to the second main expansion of the ''XY Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Wild Blaze''', the second expansion in the Pokémon Card Game XY Era. It is based on [[Pokémon X and Y]], featuring [[Generation VI]] Pokémon and the Flame Pokémon {{p|Charizard}} in both its [[Mega Evolution|Mega Evolved]] forms. The English expansion was released on May 7, 2014, while the Japanese expansion was released on March 15, 2014. Flashfire is composed of its Japanese equivalent as well as the {{TCG|M Charizard-EX Mega Battle Deck}}.

{{TCG|Secret card|Secret}} prints of M Pokémon-EX were introduced. It featured golden text of its attack in the artwork. International prints were still displayed in Japanese text, while Japanese prints were also displayed in Japanese text (as opposed to English text on Regular prints).

