'''Pokémon TCG: ''Sword & Shield—Fusion Strike''''' (Japanese: '''フュージョンアーツ''' ''Fusion Arts'') is the name given to the eighth main expansion of cards from the Sword & Shield Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] (the Sword & Shield Era in Japan). The expansion introduces the {{TCG|Fusion Strike style}} to accompany the established {{TCG|Single Strike style|Single Strike}} and {{TCG|Rapid Strike style}} mechanics.

==Blurb==
<i>Styles Combine in a New Strategy!

The road ahead reveals limitless potential as the new Fusion Strike style emerges to harness the unbound spirit of Pokémon and Trainers alike! Adaptable new Pokémon V like Genesect V, Hoopa V, and Mew VMAX are eager for battle, while Single Strike and Rapid Strike Pokémon loom large as Rillaboom VMAX, Cinderace VMAX, and Inteleon VMAX appear in their Gigantamax forms. Go with the flow and discover powerful new strategies in Pokémon TCG: Sword & Shield—Fusion Strike!</i>

==Information==
[[File:S8 Logo.png|200px|thumb|Japanese Fusion Arts logo]]
'''Fusion Strike''' is the eighth main Sword & Shield Series expansion of the Pokémon Trading Card Game and was released on November 12, 2021. In Japan, it was released as '''Fusion Arts''' on September 24, 2021 and was the eighth expansion of the Pokémon Card Game Sword & Shield Era. Fusion Strike consists of cards sourced from the Japanese Fusion Arts expansion, the {{TCG|High-Class Decks}}, the {{TCG|Sword & Shield Family Pokémon Card Game}} set, cards from {{TCG|Eevee Heroes}}, {{TCG|Skyscraping Perfection}}, and {{TCG|Blue Sky Stream}} that were not localized in {{TCG|Evolving Skies}}, and several {{TCG|S-P Promotional cards}}. Each Fusion Strike booster pack contains ten cards from the expansion and a basic {{TCG|Energy card}}. Fusion Strike booster packs were also the first to include a code card for use with the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Live]]. Each Fusion Arts pack contains five cards.

The expansion centers on the New Species Pokémon {{p|Mew}}, which is featured on {{TCG|Pokémon V}} and {{TCG|Pokémon VMAX}} cards, and is one of numerous Pokémon to support the {{TCG|Fusion Strike style}}. Fusion Strike Pokémon are designed to interact with one another, as well as supporting {{TCG|Trainer card|Trainer}} and {{TCG|Energy card}}s, to bolster a player's attacking potential while also impeding their opponent.

At 284 cards, Fusion Strike held the record for the largest expansion in the English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, and Portuguese languages, until it was surpassed by the {{TCG|Ascended Heroes}} expansion on January 30, 2026.

