'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Journey Together''''' is the name of the ninth main expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released in English on March 28, 2025.

==Blurb==
<i>Trainer's Pokémon Break into Battle!

With deep trust and steady guidance, Trainers help bring out the best in their Pokémon. The bond they share empowers them to act as one in battle as they push their strength to the limit, including as Pokémon ex! Team up with N's Zoroark ex, Iono's Bellibolt ex, Lillie's Clefairy ex, Hop's Zacian ex, and more Trainer's Pokémon, and discover the unstoppable power of friendship in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Journey Together expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Journey Together''' is the ninth main expansion of cards for the Scarlet & Violet Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. It sees the return of {{TCG|Trainer's Pokémon}} to the game, marking the first time since {{TCG|EX Team Magma vs Team Aqua}} that the mechanic has been featured in a main expansion. It focuses on Pokémon owned by four Trainers: [[N]], [[Iono]], [[Lillie]], and [[Hop]].

Journey Together includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Battle Partners}} expansion, as well as several cards from the {{TCG|Generations Start Decks}}. It contains four Trainer's {{TCG|Pokémon ex}}, 16 regular Pokémon ex, 11 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon, six {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon, and three {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

The expansion marks the return of the {{TCG|Box Topper}}, a special card included inside ''select'' booster boxes. Journey Together features two kinds of booster boxes, an '''Enhanced Booster Display Box''' that includes a specially stamped variant of the in-set {{TCG ID|Journey Together|N's Reshiram|167}} illustration rare, and a regular '''Booster Display Box''' that doesn't contain the Box Topper. Distribution for the different booster boxes is as follows:
* The Enhanced Booster Display Box was made available via the {{OBP|Pokémon Center|store}} online store.
* American [[Play! Pokémon]] retailers receive Enhanced Booster Display Boxes to sell and regular booster boxes as tournament prizing.
* European Play! Pokémon retailers have the option to sell either the Enhanced Booster Display Box or the regular booster box. 
* Non-Play! Pokémon retailers worldwide, including Best Buy<ref>[https://www.bestbuy.com/site/pokemon-trading-card-game-scarlet-violet-journey-together-booster-box-36-packs/6614262.p?skuId=6614262 Best Buy webstore]</ref> and [[GameStop]]<ref>[https://www.gamestop.com/toys-games/trading-cards/products/pokemon-trading-card-game-scarlet-and-violet-journey-together-booster-box-36-count/420197.html GameStop westore]</ref> in the {{pmin|United States}}, only have regular booster boxes available for purchase.

Journey Together is available in English, German, French, Italian, Spanish from Spain, Portuguese, and—for the first time in Pokémon TCG history—{{pmin|Latin America}}n Spanish, with all Rares and below also available as Reverse Holofoil versions.

