'''Sun & Moon: Legendary Clash''' is the name given to the sixth and final Asian Sun & Moon Era catch-up sets in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It is exclusively available in Traditional Chinese and {{pmin|Thailand|Thai}}. The Indonesian counterpart collection to this set is the {{ATCG|Tag Team Collection}}. It is the fourth expansion to be released in Traditional Chinese.

==Information==
[[File:Legendary Clash Logo Thai.png|thumb|left|170px|Thai logo]]
'''Legendary Clash''' was released on April 10, 2020 in Taiwan and Hong Kong, followed by a release in Thailand on May 24, 2020. It is an amalgamation of the final Japanese Sun & Moon Era expansions {{TCG|Miracle Twin}} and {{TCG|Alter Genesis}}, as well as the {{TCG|Sky Legend}}, {{TCG|Remix Bout}}, and {{TCG|Dream League}} subsets. It is split into two sets, Set A and Set B, each of which focuses on specific types. Set A focuses on {{TCG|Grass}}, {{TCG|Psychic}}, {{TCG|Darkness}}, {{TCG|Fairy}}, and {{ct|Dragon}} Pokémon, while Set B focuses on {{TCG|Fire}}, {{TCG|Water}}, {{TCG|Lightning}}, {{TCG|Fighting}}, {{TCG|Metal}}, and {{ct|Dragon}} Pokémon. Both sets also feature a number of {{TCG|TAG TEAM}} {{TCG|Pokémon-GX}}; {{TCG ID|Legendary Clash|Mewtwo & Mew-GX|42}} and {{TCG ID|Legendary Clash|Arceus & Dialga & Palkia-GX|131}} are featured on the booster pack art for Set A and Set B, respectively, and were specially illustrated by [[Mitsuhiro Arita]]. Each pack contains six cards.

