'''Pokémon TCG: ''Diamond & Pearl—Majestic Dawn''''' is the name given to the fifth main expansion of cards from the Diamond & Pearl Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The set continues to feature [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>Far From All Things Ordinary, the Majestic Dawn Rises

A new day is emerging for the awesome powers that wait just beyond the horizon. In the Pokémon TCG: Diamond & Pearl—Majestic Dawn expansion, the Evolution Pokémon Eevee is ready to be discovered in its ice and grass forms—Glaceon and Leafeon. With more new Pokémon, new Pokémon LV.X, a cool new Stadium card, and all seven powerful evolutions of Eevee, Majestic Dawn puts amazing origins right before your eyes!</i>

==Information==
'''Majestic Dawn''' is the name given to the fifth main expansion of the ''Diamond & Pearl Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It is based on {{game|Diamond and Pearl|s}}, featuring [[Generation IV]] Pokémon. It was released on May 21, 2008.

In North America, prerelease events were held during the weekends of May 10th–11th and May 17th–18th.<ref>https://web.archive.org/web/20080614042451/http://op.pokemon-tcg.com/events/locator/?event_type=57&location=north_america</ref>

Due to the six-month gap between the release of the fourth expansion block ({{TCG|Moonlit Pursuit}} and {{TCG|Dawn Dash}}) and the fifth expansion block ({{TCG|Cry from the Mysterious}} and {{TCG|Temple of Anger}}), Moonlit Pursuit and Dawn Dash were separated into two English expansions. Majestic Dawn mostly contained cards from the Dawn Dash expansion.

