'''Mega Brave''' (Japanese: '''メガブレイブ''') and '''Mega Symphonia''' (Japanese: '''メガシンフォニア''') are the names given to the two Japanese paired sets that collectively make up the first expansion of cards released during the Japanese [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s MEGA Series. These sets feature the [[Mega Evolution]] Pokémon Mega {{p|Lucario}} and Mega {{p|Gardevoir}}.

==Information==
'''Mega Brave''' and '''Mega Symphonia''' reintroduce [[Mega Evolution]] into the card game for the first time since the XY Series and Sun & Moon Series, as powerful Mega Evolution {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} cards worth 3 Prize cards, utilizing the typical stage and Pokémon Evolution of their depicted Pokémon. This variant of Pokémon ex uses a black-and-yellow {{Mega ex}} symbol. The first cards, Mega Lucario ex and Mega Gardevoir ex, were revealed in the [[Pokémon Presents]] presentation on [[Pokémon Day]] 2025 with a standalone trailer.<ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=REcq6yy_Ugs Pokémon TCG: Mega Evolution Series | Official Announcement Trailer]</ref> Mega Brave and Mega Symphonia also introduce {{TCG|Full Art card|Full Art}} {{rar|SR}} (SR/Super Rare, equivalent to English's {{rar|Ultra Rare}} ultra rare) prints of {{TCG|Item card}}s, {{TCG|Pokémon Tool card}}s, and {{TCG|Stadium card}}s for the first time.

A new rarity introduced in these sets is the {{rar|MUR}} (MUR/Mega Ultra Rare) rarity, applied to special gold-etched Mega Evolution Pokémon ex cards. Unlike previous Pokémon ex cards with the rarity of {{rar|UR}} (UR/Ultra Rare; Hyper Rare in English), the artworks on MUR-rarity cards are not reused from their SR counterparts; instead, they feature unique artworks with the Mega-Evolved Pokémon standing in front of elaborate circular backgrounds.

Mega Brave and Mega Symphonia are released in Japan on August 1, 2025. Each booster pack contains 5 cards. Each booster box contains 30 {{TCG|booster pack}}s. Cards within these sets are included in the English {{TCG|Mega Evolution}} expansion. The Indonesian and Thai equivalent of this set, also titled {{ATCG|Mega Evolution}}, was released on September 26, 2025.

Mega Brave and Mega Symphonia are also released in {{pmin|Chinese|Traditional Chinese}} on August 15, 2025, and in {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} on September 26, 2025. For the Traditional Chinese release in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}}, a new type of product known as the "10-Pack Set Plus" was introduced, which contains 10 booster packs (5 Mega Brave and 5 Mega Symphonia), a cardboard deck case, and a promo card pack. The promo card pack contains one random selection of three sets of Holofoil {{TCTCG|M-P Promotional cards|M-P Promotional}} Pokémon cards with the Mega Brave or Mega Symphonia logo on the artwork, plus 5 Basic Energy cards matching the Pokémon's types. The M-P Promo selection are as follows:
* Grass set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Bulbasaur|1}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Ivysaur|2}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Celebi|3}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Grass Energy}}
* Psychic set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Abra|4}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Ralts|5}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Kirlia|6}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Psychic Energy}}
* Fighting set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Makuhita|7}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Riolu|8}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Marshadow|9}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Fighting Energy}}

There are no {{TCG|Lightning}}- or {{ct|Dragon}} Pokémon in Mega Brave. Likewise, there are no {{TCG|Fighting}}-, {{TCG|Darkness}}-, or {{ct|Metal}} Pokémon in Mega Symphonia.

