'''Mega Evolution''' is the first main expansion of cards from the Asian Mega Evolution Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], released exclusively in {{pmin|Indonesia}} and {{pmin|Thailand}}. It is an adaptation of the Japanese {{TCG|Mega Brave/Mega Symphonia}} expansions.

==Information==
'''Mega Evolution''', known in Indonesian as '''Evolusi Mega''' and in Thai as '''วิวัฒนาการเมก้า''', is the first main expansion of cards for the Asian Mega Evolution Series of the {{PTCG}}, exclusively released in Indonesia and Thailand. It contains cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Mega Brave/Mega Symphonia}} expansions, and thus the set composition resembles {{TCG|Mega Evolution|the English expansion with the same name}}. The expansion introduces [[Mega Evolution]] into the Indonesian and Thai metagame for the first time as {{TCG|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} cards, each of which is worth 3 {{TCG|Prize card}}s on defeat and features the typical stage and [[Evolution]] of its depicted Pokémon. This variant of Pokémon ex uses a black-and-yellow {{Mega ex}} symbol. Each booster pack of Mega Evolution contains 5 cards.

Mega Evolution releases in Thailand on September 12, 2025, and in Indonesia on September 26, 2025. Besides being sold in individual boosters and boxes of 30 packs, Mega Evolution is also available in 2-pack blisters known as "Special Set" (Indonesian: '''Set Spesial'''; Thai: '''สเปเชียลเซ็ต'''). Special Set blisters are exclusively sold from September 22, 2025 in convenience store chain {{wp|7-Eleven}} in Thailand, and from October 1, 2025 in convenience store chain {{wp|Indomaret}} in Indonesia. Each Special Set contains a Holo promo card of {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Chikorita|1}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Scorbunny|2}}, or {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Sobble|3}} with the Indonesian/Thai Mega Evolution logo stamped on the bottom right corner of the artwork.

For the Indonesian release, a new type of product known as the "10-Pack Set Plus" (Indonesian: Set 10 Pak PLUS) was also introduced, adapting the Taiwan and Hong Kong product of the same name. The Mega Evolution 10-Pack Set Plus contains 10 booster packs, a cardboard deck case, and a promo card pack. The promo card pack contains one random selection of three sets of Holofoil {{ITCG|M-P Promotional cards|M-P Promotional}} Pokémon cards with the Mega Evolution logo on the artwork, plus 5 Basic Energy cards matching the Pokémon's types. The M-P Promo selection are as follows:
* Grass set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Bulbasaur|1}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Ivysaur|2}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Celebi|3}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Grass Energy}}
* Psychic set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Abra|4}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Ralts|5}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Kirlia|6}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Psychic Energy}}
* Fighting set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Makuhita|7}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Riolu|8}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Marshadow|9}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Fighting Energy}}

