'''Pokémon TCG: ''Mega Evolution''''' is the first main expansion of cards from the Mega Evolution Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]].

==Blurb==
<i>Mega Evolve Your Strength to the Next Stage!

Striving to become stronger, Pokémon of all types are putting everything on the line to become Mega Evolution Pokémon ex! Harness the strong aura of Mega Lucario ex, embrace the overflowing power of Mega Gardevoir ex, and team up with more of these powerful Pokémon that boast devastating attacks and massive HP. But consider your strategy carefully—extra power brings extra risks! Choose your Pokémon partners and prepare for the biggest battles you’ve ever seen in the Pokémon TCG: Mega Evolution expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Mega Evolution''' is the first main expansion of cards for the Mega Evolution Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. It reintroduces [[Mega Evolution]] into the game as {{TCG|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} cards, each of which is worth 3 {{TCG|Prize card}}s on defeat and features the typical stage and [[Evolution]] of its depicted Pokémon. This variant of Pokémon ex uses a black-and-yellow {{Mega ex}} symbol.

Most of the cards in this set come from the Japanese {{TCG|Mega Brave}} and {{TCG|Mega Symphonia}} expansions, with a few reprinted Trainer cards first released in the Japanese {{TCG|Premium Trainer Box MEGA}}. Starting with this expansion, {{TCG|Item}}, {{TCG|Pokémon Tool}}, and {{TCG|Stadium card|Stadium}} cards cards can appear as full-art {{TCG|ultra rare}} cards;<ref name="TCG 230625"/> the first of these to be revealed were {{TCG ID|Mega Evolution|Night Stretcher|173}} and {{TCG ID|Mega Evolution|Rare Candy|175}}.<ref name="YT 230625"/> Mega Evolution also reintroduces Mirror Holofoil variants of cards, last seen during the {{TCG|Black & White}} Series.

Mega Evolution features 188 cards in total, including 10 Mega Evolution Pokémon ex, more than 15 Trainer cards, 22 illustration rare Pokémon cards, 22 ultra rare Mega Evolution Pokémon ex and Trainer cards, and 10 special illustration rare Mega Evolution Pokémon ex and Supporter cards.<ref name="TCG 100725"/><ref name="TPCi 100725"/>

Mega Evolution released globally on September 26, 2025, although the release in the Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA) regions was delayed to October 10, 2025 due to product delivery problems.<ref>(27 August 2025). "[https://www.pokemon.com/uk/pokemon-news/important-notice-about-the-upcoming-pokemon-tcg-mega-evolution-expansion Important Notice About the Upcoming Pokémon TCG: Mega Evolution Expansion]." Pokemon.com (UK)</ref>

