'''Scarlet & Violet: Miracle Journey''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 奇迹启程''') is the second {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet Series, and the tenth main expansion overall.

== Information ==
'''Miracle Journey''' is the second Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game and continues to introduce more [[Generation IX]] Pokémon to the game. Most of its cards originate from the Japanese {{TCG|Scarlet ex}}, {{TCG|Violet ex}}, and {{TCG|Triplet Beat}} subsets, with a small number of {{TCG|Pokémon Card 151}} and promotional cards also included. The expansion focuses on {{OBP|Gardevoir ex|Miracle Journey 55}} and the final Evolutions of [[Paldea]]'s [[Paldea first partner Pokémon|first partner Pokémon]]: {{OBP|Meowscarada ex|Miracle Journey 12}}, {{OBP|Skeledirge ex|Miracle Journey 21}}, and {{OBP|Quaquaval ex|Miracle Journey 33}}.

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 115 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and one with a rarer Master Ball motif.

