'''Pokémon TCG: ''Diamond & Pearl—Mysterious Treasures''''' (Japanese: '''湖の秘密''' ''Secret of the Lakes'') is the name given to the second main expansion of cards from the Diamond & Pearl Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] (the DP Era in Japan). The set continues to feature [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>Seek New Pokémon and You Shall Find... Mysterious Treasures

The search for new Pokémon continues! In Mysterious Treasures, you'll catch the next wave of brand-new Pokémon that no Trainer has ever caught before. You'll find new gameplay options like Pokémon with Berries, new Fossils, more powerful Pokémon LV.X, and attacks that will change the way every Trainer plays. You will treasure the power when you play the Pokémon TCG: Diamond & Pearl—Mysterious Treasures expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Mysterious Treasures''' is the name given to the second main expansion of the ''Diamond & Pearl Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Secret of the Lakes''', the second expansion in the Pokémon Card Game DP Era. It is based on {{game|Diamond and Pearl|s}}, featuring [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and the [[lake guardians]] {{p|Uxie}}, {{p|Mesprit}}, and {{p|Azelf}}. The English expansion was released on August 22, 2007, while the Japanese expansion was released on March 2, 2007.

In North America, prerelease events were held during the weekends of August 11th-12th, 18th-19th, and 25th-26th.<ref>https://web.archive.org/web/20070911223031/http://op.pokemon-tcg.com/events/locator/?event_type=47&location=north_america</ref>

Mysterious Treasures introduced Pokémon that come with held items. The effect stays active whenever the Pokémon is in play.

