'''Mystical Seven''' (Korean: '''7개의 신비''' ''7-gae-ui Sinbi'') is the name given to the fifth extension set of cards from the DP Series of the {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The set continues to feature {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}}. Despite having a large range of types, this set focuses on {{ct|Grass}} and {{ct|Water}} cards.

==Information==
'''Mystical Seven''' is the fifth Korean extension set of cards after the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] went into hiatus until the middle of 2010. Released October 14, 2010, this extension set continues to introduce both new [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and new {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the Korean Card Game. Having {{p|Leafeon}} and {{p|Glaceon}} under its spotlight, this set focuses on {{ct|Grass}} and {{ct|Water}} cards.

Included in the Mystical Seven set are 40 cards originating from the early half of the English Diamond & Pearl Series. The set pulls its Ultra-Rare {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} focus from the {{TCG|Majestic Dawn}} expansion and contains a majority of cards from the {{TCG|Diamond & Pearl}} and {{TCG|Majestic Dawn}} expansions.

The only [[Legendary Pokémon]] included in the set is {{p|Deoxys}}, which is present in its four different forms.

