'''Nihil Zero''' (Japanese: '''ムニキスゼロ''' ''Munikisu Zero'') is the name given to the third expansion of cards released during the Japanese [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s MEGA Series. This set is based on the video game [[Pokémon Legends: Z-A]] and features [[Mega Evolution|Mega]] {{p|Zygarde}}. ''Munikisu Zero'' was localized on the English {{TCG ID|Perfect Order|Mega Zygarde ex|47}} card as '''Nullifying Zero'''.

==Information==
'''Nihil Zero''' is the first booster set to be fully based on the video game [[Pokémon Legends: Z-A]] (although there have been cards based on Pokémon and characters from the video game in products released prior). The central Pokémon is {{TCG ID|Nihil Zero|Mega Zygarde ex|46}}, appearing as a {{TCG|Pokémon ex|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} card. Various other Pokémon and characters from Pokémon Legends: Z-A also appear as cards.

Nihil Zero was released in {{pmin|Japan}} on January 23, 2026, followed by localized releases in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}} on February 6, 2026, and in {{pmin|South Korea}} on March 13, 2026. Each booster pack contains 5 cards. Each booster box contains 30 packs. Cards released in this set are included in the English {{TCG|Perfect Order}} expansion.

For the Traditional Chinese release in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}}, the "10-Pack Set Plus" product is available, which contains 10 booster packs, a cardboard deck case, and a promo card pack. The promo card pack contains one random selection of three sets of Holofoil {{TCTCG|M-P Promotional cards|M-P Promotional}} Pokémon cards with the Nihil Zero logo on the artwork, plus 5 Basic Energy cards. The M-P Promo selection are as follows:
* Grass set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Shaymin|62}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Rowlet|63}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Dartrix|64}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Grass Energy}}
* Water set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Seel|65}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Staryu|66}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Volcanion|67}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Water Energy}}
* Psychic set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Clefairy|68}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Mawile|69}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Spritzee|70}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Psychic Energy}}

The set's Japanese name, Munikisu Zero, references the Japanese name of Mega Zygarde's [[signature move]], {{m|Nihil Light}} (Japanese: 無に帰す光 ''Munikisu Hikari''). The name also forms the initialism "MZ", which alludes to two important Pokémon Legends: Z-A elements, namely [[Team MZ]] and Mega Zygarde.

