'''Ninja Spinner''' (Japanese: '''ニンジャスピナー''' ''Ninja Spinner'') is the name given to the fourth expansion of cards released during the Japanese [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s MEGA Series. This set features [[Mega Evolution|Mega]] {{p|Greninja}} as the central Pokémon.

==Information==
'''Ninja Spinner''' continues to introduce {{TCG|Pokémon ex|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} and Trainer cards based on the video game {{g|Legends: Z-A}} to the Pokémon Trading Card Game. The set primarily focuses on the [[Kalos first partner Pokémon]], with {{TCG ID|Ninja Spinner|Mega Greninja ex|22}} as the central Pokémon; as well as the final act of the Pokémon Legends: Z-A game, with cards based on {{me|Floette}} and [[Ange]].

Ninja Spinner was released in {{pmin|Japan}} on March 13, 2026, followed by localized releases in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}} on March 27, 2026, and in {{pmin|South Korea}} on May 1, 2026. Each booster pack contains 5 cards. Each booster box contains 30 packs. Cards released in this set are included in the English {{TCG|Chaos Rising}} expansion.

