'''Pokémon TCG: ''Mega Evolution—Perfect Order''''' is the third main expansion of cards from the Mega Evolution Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The expansion is themed after the video game [[Pokémon Legends: Z-A]] and introduces Mega {{p|Zygarde}} ex as the central Pokémon. It released on March 27, 2026.

==Blurb==
<i><b>Secret Powers Awaken!</b>

The pulse of the city beats in sync with the Pokémon and people who call it home—and preserving the order of it all is Mega Zygarde ex, the Legendary Pokémon who embodies strength in numbers! With threatening forces held at bay, peaceful days are ahead for the city’s residents, including Pokémon like Mega Clefable ex, Mega Starmie ex, and Meowth ex, in the Pokémon TCG: </i>Mega Evolution—Perfect Order<i> expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Perfect Order''' is the third main expansion of cards for the Mega Evolution Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. It is the first main set to be based on the video game {{g|Legends: Z-A}}, and the second overall after {{TCG|Ascended Heroes}}. {{TCG ID|Perfect Order|Mega Zygarde ex|47}} stands as the central Pokémon of the set, accompanied by cards themed around the Pokémon Legends: Z-A video game such as {{TCG ID|Perfect Order|Lumiose City|77}}.<ref name="TPCi 20260108"/>

Perfect Order includes cards released in the Japanese {{TCG|Nihil Zero}} expansion. Perfect Order features more than 120 cards, including four Mega Evolution Pokémon ex; nine Pokémon ex; 11 illustration rare Pokémon; 18 ultra rare Pokémon and Trainer cards; and six special illustration rare Pokémon and Supporter cards.<ref name="TPCi 20260108"/> In the English set and the languages following the English set structure, all Rares and below are also available as Reverse Holofoil versions.

Perfect Order released worldwide on March 27, 2026.<ref name="TPCi 20260108"/>

