'''Pokémon TCG: ''Mega Evolution—Phantasmal Flames''''' is the second main expansion of cards from the Mega Evolution Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The expansion continues to introduce [[Mega Evolution]] Pokémon cards into the game, with Mega {{p|Charizard}} X ex as the central Pokémon. It was released on November 14, 2025.

==Blurb==
<i><b>Ignite a Burning Spirit of Battle!</b>

Searing blue flames rip across a dark battlefield as Mega Charizard X ex soars up and looks down upon its opponents! With a deep chill to rival the heat, the shadowy figure of Mega Gengar ex slowly rises into view, and both Pokémon prepare to attack. Determined to prove their mettle, Mega Heracross ex, Mega Lopunny ex, and even more Pokémon line up to give it their all in the Pokémon TCG: </i>Mega Evolution—Phantasmal Flames<i> expansion!</i>

==Information==
'''Phantasmal Flames''' is the second main expansion of cards for the Mega Evolution Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. It continues to introduce {{TCG|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} cards into the game, with {{TCG ID|Phantasmal Flames|Mega Charizard X ex|13}} as the central Pokémon. {{TCG ID|MEGA Starter Set|Mega Gengar ex|3}} and other Mega Evolution Pokémon ex, as well as regular Pokémon ex, are also included. Overall, the set focuses on {{ct|Fire}} and {{ct|Darkness}} Pokémon.<ref name="TPCi 20250905"/>

Phantasmal Flames includes cards released in the Japanese {{TCG|Inferno X}} expansion, as well as the {{TCG|MEGA Starter Set Mega Gengar ex}} and the {{TCG|MEGA Starter Set Mega Diancie ex}}. Phantasmal Flames features 130 cards, including six Mega Evolution Pokémon ex; four Pokémon ex; 13 illustration rare Pokémon; 17 ultra rare Mega Evolution Pokémon ex, Trainer and Energy cards; and five special illustration rare Mega Evolution Pokémon ex and Supporter cards.<ref name="TPCi 20250905"/> In the English set and the languages following the English set structure, all Rares and below are also available as Reverse Holofoil versions.

Phantasmal Flames was released worldwide on November 14, 2025.<ref name="TPCi 20250905"/>

