'''Pokémon TCG: ''XY—Phantom Forces''''' (Japanese: '''ファントムゲート''' ''Phantom Gate'') is the name given to the fourth main expansion of cards from the XY Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] (the XY Era in Japan). The set continues to feature [[Generation VI]] Pokémon, {{TCG|Pokémon-EX|Pokémon-EX, and M Pokémon-EX}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>Master Mysterious Powers!

Gather your courage and peer into the haunted void with the Pokémon TCG: XY—Phantom Forces expansion! Mega Manectric-EX makes a shocking appearance to light the way, while the ghostly grin of Mega Gengar-EX frightens challengers near and far. Take along Aegislash-EX to give you an edge, push the limits of Mega Evolution with new Skill Link cards, and call on all of your Trainer knowledge to escape the eerie forces at work!</i>
{{-}}

==Information==
[[File:XY4 Logo.png|200px|thumb|Phantom Gate logo]]
'''Phantom Forces''' is the name given to the fourth main expansion of the ''XY Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Phantom Gate''', the fourth expansion in the Pokémon Card Game XY Era. It is based on [[Pokémon X and Y]], featuring [[Generation VI]] Pokémon and the Shadow Pokémon {{p|Gengar}}. The English expansion was released on November 5, 2014, while the Japanese expansion was released on September 13, 2014.

Phantom Forces introduced Spirit Link, {{TCG|Pokémon Tool card}}s that allowed Pokémon to Mega Evolve without ending the player's turn.

The set has a light [[Team Flare]] theme, featuring major characters as {{TCG|Supporter card}}s, a group of {{TCG|Item card}}s designated as '''Team Flare Gear''' and two Pokémon Tool cards that are {{TCG|Team Flare Hyper Gear}}. The Team Flare Hyper Gear cards are unique as Tools that are attached to the opponent's Pokémon in order to hinder them.

