'''Pokémon Web''' (Japanese: '''ポケモンカード★web''' ''Pokémon Card★web'') is the only main expansion of cards from the web Era of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game|Pokémon Card Game]] in Japan. It does not have a main expansion as an English equivalent.

==Information==
'''Pokémon Card★web''' is the only expansion in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game|Pokémon Card Game]] web Era. It was released on October 20, 2001.

The expansion split the {{TCG|Pokémon Power}} mechanic into two groups; Poké-Power and Poké-Body. Poké-Powers require activation to use, whereas Poké-Bodies are always active unless blocked by specific interactions. This was also the first expansion to feature {{TCG|Supporter card}}s, following up on the {{TCG ID|P Promo|Bill|9}} {{TCG|P Promotional cards|P Promotional card}} released the previous month.

Pokémon Card★web is composed of reprints of the {{TCG|Expansion Pack}}, {{TCG|Pokémon Jungle}}, {{TCG|Mystery of the Fossils}}, and {{TCG|Rocket Gang}} expansions, as well as several promotional cards. The reprints are updated to reflect the new mechanics. For example, {{TCG ID|Pokémon Web|Dragonite|38}}'s ''Special Delivery'' is now classified as a Poké-Power, and {{TCG ID|Pokémon Web|Rocket's Sneak Attack|40}} is now a Supporter card. The cards utilize the card design introduced in {{TCG|Pokémon VS|Pokémon Card★VS}}. The set symbol is located on the bottom left of the card, and the back of the card also utilizes the current "Pokémon" design. 

Pokémon Card★web booster packs could be purchased online exclusively on the [[Pokémon Center (store)#Japan 3|Pokémon Center Online]]. Each pack contained ten cards, nine Non Holofoil and one Holofoil. The cards were packaged in clear plastic with a barcoded cover card featuring the set logo as opposed to traditional foil boosters.

