'''Scarlet & Violet: Presence of Champions''' is the name given to the special set released in the Asian Scarlet & Violet Era of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It is an {{pmin|Indonesia}}- and {{pmin|Thailand}}-exclusive adaptation of {{TCG|Hot Wind Arena}} and {{TCG|Glory of the Rocket Gang}}, the ninth subset and the tenth main TCG expansion of Japanese Scarlet & Violet Era, respectively.

==Information==
'''Presence of Champions''', known in Indonesian as '''Kehadiran Juara''' and in Thai as '''การผงาดของผู้ไร้พ่าย''', is a special set exclusive to Indonesia and Thailand released for the Asian Scarlet & Violet Era of the {{PTCG}}. It is the eighth such set for the Indonesian market, and the fourth such set for the Thai market. It is largely an adaptation of the Japanese {{TCG|Hot Wind Arena}} and {{TCG|Glory of the Rocket Gang}} expansions, which includes {{TCG|Trainer's Pokémon}} to the Scarlet & Violet Era. Those Trainer's Pokémon belong to [[Misty]], {{ga|Ethan}}, [[Cynthia]], [[Arven]], or [[Team Rocket]] ([[Giovanni]], his {{tc|Executive}}s, and his {{tc|Team Rocket Grunt|Grunts}}). Each booster pack of Presence of Champions contains 5 cards.

Presence of Champions is set to be released in Thailand on June 13, 2025, and in Indonesia on May 30, 2025. A Collector's Set (Indonesian: Set Kolektor) for Presence of Champions was available for sale at the same time as the set's release in Indonesia. The Indonesian Presence of Champions Collector's Set contains 10 booster packs, a card list booklet, and a stamped Full Art promo card of Meowth.

