'''Space-Time Clash''' (Korean: '''시공의 격돌''' ''Sigong-ui Gyeokdol'') is the name given to the third extension set of cards from the DP Series of the {{pmin|South Korea|Korean}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. The set continues to feature {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} for the Korean Card Game. This set focuses on the types that were missing from the previous sets, {{ct|Psychic}}, {{ct|Fighting}}, {{ct|Darkness}}, and {{ct|Metal}}.

==Information==
'''Space-Time Clash''' is the third Korean extension set of cards after the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] went into hiatus until the middle of 2010. Released August 26, 2010, this extension set continues to introduce both new [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and new {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} in the Korean Card Game. In order to give the players what was missing from the previous set, this set focuses on releasing {{ct|Psychic}}, {{ct|Fighting}}, {{ct|Darkness}}, and {{ct|Metal}} cards.

Included in the Space-Time Clash set are 60 cards originating from the early half of the English Diamond & Pearl Series. The set pulls its {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}} from the {{TCG|Great Encounters}} and {{TCG|Legends Awakened}} expansions, but contains a majority of cards from the {{TCG|Diamond & Pearl}} and {{TCG|Legends Awakened}} expansions.

The only three [[Legendary Pokémon]] included in the set are {{p|Palkia}}, {{p|Dialga}}, and {{p|Giratina}}. Palkia and Dialga are included twice ({{TCG ID|Diamond & Pearl|Palkia|11}} and {{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Palkia LV.X|106}}, {{TCG ID|Diamond & Pearl|Dialga|1}} and {{TCG ID|Great Encounters|Dialga LV.X|105}}). {{TCG|Darkness Energy}} and {{TCG|Metal Energy}} premier in this extension.

