'''Scarlet & Violet: Stellar Crystal''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 星彩晶璃''') is the ninth {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet Series.

== Information ==
[[File:CSV9 banner.png|thumb|300px|Set banner artwork]]
'''Stellar Crystal''' is the ninth Scarlet & Violet expansion to be released in the Simplified Chinese language version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. The expansion introduces elements from [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]]'s [[The Indigo Disk]] expansion, including [[Pokémon ex (TCG)#Tera Pokémon ex|Stellar Tera Pokémon ex]], a special type of Tera Pokémon ex featuring {{Tera}}stallized Pokémon with the {{t|Stellar}} type. It also includes new Pokémon introduced in the expansion, such as {{p|Terapagos}} and {{p|Archaludon}}, and new characters, such as [[Briar]], [[Lacey]], and [[Crispin]]. Most of the set's cards originate from the Japanese {{TCG|Stellar Miracle}} and {{TCG|Super Electric Breaker}} sets, as well as a small number from other sets and products.

Stellar Crystal features one card exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language: a {{TCG|special illustration rare}} print of {{TCG|Lisia's Appeal}}.

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 177 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and a rarer one with a Master Ball motif.

