'''Storm Emeralda''' (Japanese: '''ストームエメラルダ''' ''Storm Emeralda'') is the name given to the sixth expansion of cards released during the Japanese [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]'s MEGA Series. This set features {{me|Rayquaza}} as the central Pokémon.

==Information==
'''Storm Emeralda''' continues to introduce {{TCG|Pokémon ex|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} and Trainer cards from the video game. Instead of being based on [[Pokémon Legends: Z-A]], this set is primarily based on [[Pokémon Omega Ruby and Alpha Sapphire]], featuring characters from the games and a heavy focus on {{TCG ID|Storm Emeralda|Mega Rayquaza ex|58}} as the central Pokémon, although [[Mega Evolution]] Pokémon from Pokémon Legends: Z-A still make an appearance.

A new gameplay mechanic introduced in this expansion is paired {{TCG|Stadium card}}s that feature one artwork split into two. These pairs of Stadium cards are played together as one large card, but otherwise follow the same rules as other Stadium cards.

Storm Emeralda is designed for use in {{TCG|Sealed format}} tournaments, in which participants are provided with sealed TCG products and have to build and battle their decks using only cards pulled from those products, along with any other cards provided by the tournament staff.

Storm Emeralda was released in {{pmin|Japan}} on July 31, 2026, followed by localized releases in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}} on August 7, 2026, and in {{pmin|South Korea}} on August 21, 2026. Each booster pack contains 5 cards. Each booster box contains 30 packs. Cards released in this set are included in the English {{TCG|Delta Reign}} expansion releasing on November 6, 2026.

Storm Emeralda was revealed at the same time as Delta Reign and {{TCGP|Ruler of the Skies}}, the latter being a Rayquaza-themed set for [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]].

