'''Pokémon TCG: ''Platinum—Supreme Victors''''' (Japanese: '''フロンティアの鼓動''' ''Beat of the Frontier'') is the name given to the third main expansion of cards from the Platinum Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] (the DPt Era in Japan). The set continues to feature [[Generation IV]] Pokémon, {{TCG|Pokémon LV.X}}, and {{TCG|Pokémon SP}} in the card game.

==Blurb==
<i>Ultimate Challenges... Supreme Victors!

Increase your power with impressive new Pokémon that will take you to the pinnacle of Pokémon battles—the Battle Frontier! In the Pokémon TCG: Platinum—Supreme Victors expansion, you'll find more sizzling Pokémon SP like Blaziken {{SP|FB}}, more ferocious Pokémon LV.X like Charizard {{SP|G}} LV.X, and more opportunities to battle your way to the top! Your victory will be supreme when you play with Pokémon trained by Team Galactic, the Frontier Brains, and the Sinnoh League Champion!</i>

==Information==
[[File:DPt3 Logo.png|200px|thumb|Beat of the Frontier logo]]
'''Supreme Victors''' is the name given to the third main expansion of the ''Platinum Series'' of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. In Japan, it was released as '''Beat of the Frontier''', the third expansion in the Pokémon Card Game DPt Era. It is based on {{game|Platinum}}, featuring [[Generation IV]] Pokémon and the [[Sinnoh]] region [[Frontier Brain]]s. The English expansion was released on August 19, 2009, while the Japanese expansion was released on March 6, 2009.

The fourth and fifth variants of {{TCG|Pokémon SP}} introduced were the Pokémon {{SP|C}} and Pokémon {{SP|FB}}, Pokémon that were owned by Cynthia and the Frontier Brains respectively. The Frontier Brain's Pokémon are Pokémon that they used in Pokémon Platinum Version.

