'''Pokémon TCG: ''Scarlet & Violet—Surging Sparks''''' is the name of the eighth main expansion of cards from the Scarlet & Violet Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It was released in English on November 8, 2024.

==Blurb==
<i>A Growing Storm of Stellar Strength!

Terawatts of electricity crash down from the sky in a tropical paradise, setting the stage for the supercharged Pikachu ex! With the power of a Stellar Tera Pokémon ex, it lights up the shoreline, revealing a parade of dragon Pokémon led by the towering Alolan Exeggutor ex! Archaludon ex and Latias ex round out the horde, while new ACE SPEC cards and more new Pokémon ex bring surprises of their own. Currents crackle and dragons roar in the Pokémon TCG: Scarlet & Violet—Surging Sparks expansion!</i>

==Information==
<!--[[File:SV8 Logo JP.png|200px|thumb|Super Electric Breaker logo]]-->
'''Surging Sparks''' makes up the eighth expansion of cards for the Scarlet & Violet Series of the Pokémon Trading Card Game. This expansion continues to introduce Stellar {{Tera}} {{TCG|Pokémon ex}} into the game, a concept first introduced in the previous {{TCG|Stellar Crown}} expansion. A running theme in the set is the [[Terarium]], the primary setting of [[The Indigo Disk]], the second part of [[The Hidden Treasure of Area Zero]] DLC for the [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]] video games.

Surging Sparks includes cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Super Electric Breaker}} and {{TCG|Paradise Dragona}} expansions, as well as the {{TCG|Stellar Tera Type Starter Sets}} and certain {{TCG|SV-P Promotional cards}}. Surging Sparks contains eight {{TCG|ACE SPEC card}}s, nine Stellar Tera Pokémon ex and nine Pokémon ex, 23 {{TCG|illustration rare}} Pokémon<!--, ?? {{TCG|ultra rare}} full-art etched Pokémon ex and Supporter cards-->, 11 {{TCG|special illustration rare}} Pokémon and Supporter cards, and six {{TCG|hyper rare}} gold etched cards.

Surging Sparks is available in English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, and Portuguese with all Rares and below also available as Reverse Holofoil versions.. <!--Super Electric Breaker is released in Japanese on ???, 2024, followed by localized releases in Traditional Chinese on ???, 2024, and in Korean on ??. The Thai and Indonesian set equivalent, {{ATCG|???}}, is released on ???.-->

