'''Sword & Shield''' is the name given to the first of three Asian Sword & Shield Era catch-up sets in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]]. It is available in {{pmin|Chinese|Traditional Chinese}}, {{pmin|Thailand|Thai}} and {{pmin|Indonesia}}n.

==Information==
'''Sword & Shield''' was first released on June 19, 2020 in {{pmin|Taiwan}} and {{pmin|Hong Kong}}, followed by releases in {{pmin|Thailand}} on September 8 and {{pmin|Indonesia}} on November 21. The set is composed of cards sourced from the dual Japanese {{TCG|Sword}} and {{TCG|Shield}} expansions, the {{TCG|Rebellion Crash}} expansion, as well as the {{TCG|VMAX Rising}} subset, featuring [[Generation VIII]] Pokémon and the {{TCG|Pokémon V|Pokémon V and Pokémon VMAX}} mechanics for the first time in their respective markets. It is split into two collections, Set A and Set B, each of which feature specific type rosters. Set A focuses on {{TCG|Lightning}}, {{TCG|Psychic}}, {{TCG|Fighting}}, and {{ct|Metal}} Pokémon, while Set B focuses on {{TCG|Grass}}, {{TCG|Fire}}, {{TCG|Water}}, and {{ct|Darkness}} Pokémon. The symbols for each set are also uniform across all three languages for the first time and feature a letter to denote their localized release. Products available in Taiwan and Hong Kong have symbols with 'F' (Fanti, traditional Chinese characters); those available in Thailand have symbols with 'T'; those available in Indonesia have symbols with 'I'. Booster packs available in all languages contain five cards.

