'''Scarlet & Violet: Together in Pursuit of Glory''' (Simplified Chinese: '''朱&紫 共逐荣光''') is the twelfth {{pmin|mainland China|Simplified Chinese}} [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] expansion of the Scarlet & Violet Series.

== Information ==
'''Together in Pursuit of Glory''' introduces {{TCG|Trainer's Pokémon}} to the Simplified Chinese version of the Pokémon Trading Card Game, primarily amalgamating the Japanese sets {{TCG|Battle Partners}}, {{TCG|Hot Wind Arena}}, and {{TCG|Glory of the Rocket Gang}}. As such, it focuses heavily on [[Team Rocket]] due to the number of Team Rocket's Pokémon featured in the set, while also including Pokémon owned by [[Arven]], [[Cynthia]], [[Ethan]], [[Hop]], [[Iono]], [[Lillie]], [[Marnie]], [[Misty]], [[N]], and [[Steven Stone]].

Together in Pursuit of Glory features one card exclusive to the Simplified Chinese language: a {{TCG|special illustration rare}} print of {{TCG|Brock's Scouting}}.

Cards are available in two different types of booster packs:

* 5-card booster packs; one card is either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} or higher;
* 20-card booster packs; six cards are either Reverse Holofoil or have a rarity of {{rar|R}} of higher.

Each of the 198 common, uncommon, and rare cards in the expansion come in two Reverse Holofoil variants - one with a Poké Ball motif, and a rarer one with a Master Ball motif.

