'''Void Blast''' is the fourth main expansion of cards from the Asian Mega Evolution Series of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], released exclusively in {{pmin|Thailand}} and {{pmin|Indonesia}}. Primarily based on the video game {{g|Legends: Z-A}}, this set adapts the Japanese {{TCG|Nihil Zero}} expansion, while also including cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Start Deck 100 Battle Collection}}.

==Information==
'''Void Blast''', known in Thai as '''วอยด์บลาสต์''' and in Indonesian as '''Ledakan Peniada''', is the fourth main expansion of cards for the Asian Mega Evolution Series of the {{PTCG}}, exclusively released in Thailand and Indonesia. It contains cards from the Japanese {{TCG|Nihil Zero}} expansion and some, but not all, cards from the {{TCG|Start Deck 100 Battle Collection}}. The expansion features various {{TCG|Mega Evolution Pokémon ex}} and Trainer cards, many of which are themed around the video game {{g|Legends: Z-A}}. The central Pokémon in the expansion are {{TCG ID|Void Blast|Mega Zygarde ex|73}} and {{TCG ID|Void Blast|Mega Charizard Y ex|25}}. Each booster pack of Void Blast contains 5 cards.

Void Blast releases in Thailand on March 20, 2026, and in Indonesia on April 3, 2026. Besides being sold in individual boosters and boxes of 30 packs, Void Blast is also available in 2-pack blisters known as "Special Set" (Indonesian: '''Set Spesial'''; Thai: '''สเปเชียลเซ็ต''').

For the Indonesian release, the "10-Pack Set Plus" (Indonesian: Set 10 Pak PLUS) product was also introduced, adapting the Taiwan and Hong Kong product of the same name. The Void Blast 10-Pack Set Plus contains 10 booster packs, a cardboard deck case, and a promo card pack. The promo card pack contains one random selection of three sets of Holofoil {{ITCG|M-P Promotional cards|M-P Promotional}} Pokémon cards with the Void Blast logo on the artwork, plus 5 Basic Energy cards matching the Pokémon's types. The M-P Promo selection are as follows:
* Grass set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Chikorita|61}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Bayleef|62}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Shaymin|63}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Grass Energy}}
* Fire set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Tepig|64}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Pignite|65}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Salandit|66}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Fire Energy}}
* Water set: {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Staryu|67}}, {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Totodile|68}}, and {{TCG ID|M-P Promo|Croconaw|69}}, plus 5 {{TCG|Basic Water Energy}}

